1
00:01:32,527 --> 00:01:37,337
اَعُوْذُ بِاللهِ مِنَّ الشِّيْطَانِ الرَّجِيْمِ۝بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمَانِ الرَّحِيْمَ۝

2
00:01:38,217 --> 00:01:44,793
اَلْحَمْدُ لله وَالصَّلَاةُ وَالسَّلَامُ عَلى سَيِّدِنَا محمد وَعَلَى اَلِهِ وَصَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ تَسْلِيْمًا كَثِيْراً

3
00:01:44,817 --> 00:01:46,261
اَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكُمْ وَرَحْمَةُ الله

4
00:01:48,709 --> 00:01:50,565
UMAR(عُمَر) AND HIS PEOPLE,

5
00:01:53,956 --> 00:02:05,830
We start first with Umar(عُمَر) and the women citizens, especially the women of Madina.

6
00:02:10,364 --> 00:02:16,086
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab رضي الله عنه was walking down a road in Madina

7
00:02:17,345 --> 00:02:24,757
accompanied with some of his advisors or followers.

8
00:02:27,548 --> 00:02:35,270
And a woman comes up to Umar(عُمَر) and she stops him and she said: O Umar(عُمَر)!

9
00:02:37,676 --> 00:02:44,565
I remember one day, you would be called Umair(عمير).

10
00:02:47,545 --> 00:02:50,555
Umair(عمير) is small Umar(عُمَر).

11
00:02:52,166 --> 00:02:55,158
It's Seeghat Tasgheera(صيغه تصغيرة) in Arabic,

12
00:02:55,355 --> 00:02:59,224
if you want to make something smaller you add that Ya(ي) to it,

13
00:03:00,057 --> 00:03:03,471
so Umar(عُمَر), Umair(عمير), Asad(اسد) Usaid(اُسيد).

14
00:03:05,497 --> 00:03:10,245
So, she said, I remember a day, when you were young,

15
00:03:11,263 --> 00:03:14,389
you would be called Umair(عمیر)

16
00:03:16,345 --> 00:03:20,329
and you would be carrying your stick with you, terrorizing the kids.

17
00:03:21,666 --> 00:03:24,233
He would go around beating the kids when you was young, with a stick.

18
00:03:26,184 --> 00:03:29,092
He was a tough man since his young days,

19
00:03:29,117 --> 00:03:33,431
he would go around the streets of Makkah fighting the kids with his stick.

20
00:03:34,284 --> 00:03:37,239
He became a wrestler after that.

21
00:03:39,412 --> 00:03:43,341
So, he was that type of street boy, when he was a young.

22
00:03:47,757 --> 00:03:52,744
Umair(عمير) and then after that, you were called Umar(عُمَر)

23
00:03:54,683 --> 00:04:00,166
and then the days passed and you are called Ameer-Ul-Mo’mineen(امير المؤمنين).

24
00:04:01,833 --> 00:04:09,433
So, fear Allah! And fear Allah with your people and remember the day of Judgment.

25
00:04:11,263 --> 00:04:13,671
And she went on giving him Naseeha(نصيحه).

26
00:04:14,348 --> 00:04:17,875
And Umar(عُمَر) just stood there listening to her without any interruption.

27
00:04:21,137 --> 00:04:23,381
So, the man with Umar(عُمَر) stopped her and he said,

28
00:04:24,783 --> 00:04:28,157
Stop speaking like that to Ameer-Ul-Mo’mineen(امير المؤمنين).

29
00:04:30,148 --> 00:04:31,907
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) said: You stop.

30
00:04:34,158 --> 00:04:40,131
If this woman would continue talking, I would continue listening

31
00:04:40,797 --> 00:04:43,988
and I would only leave her to go and make Salah(صلاة) and come back.

32
00:04:46,682 --> 00:04:48,941
Why shouldn’t I listen to a woman

33
00:04:49,617 --> 00:04:55,346
whom Allahعَزّوجَلّ listened to her complains from above seven heavens.

34
00:04:56,857 --> 00:05:02,453
This was Khawlah(خوله), who went to complain about her husband to Rasool Allah ﷺ

35
00:05:03,704 --> 00:05:07,298
and Ayesha(عائشه) said; I was in the next room and I could barely

36
00:05:07,675 --> 00:05:10,908
hear the conversation between Rasool Allah ﷺ and her

37
00:05:11,503 --> 00:05:15,333
but Allahعَزّوجَلّ heard her and revealed Ayaat(آيات):

38
00:05:15,357 --> 00:05:21,887
قَدْ سَمِعَ اللَّهُ قَوْلَ الَّتِي تُجَادِلُكَ فِي زَوْجِهَا وَتَشْتَكِي إِلَى اللَّهِ وَاللّهُ يَسْمَعُ تَحَاوُرَكُمَا

39
00:05:22,823 --> 00:05:26,811
 Allahعَزّوجَلّ heard the conversation of the woman,

40
00:05:26,835 --> 00:05:33,624
who was complaining to you about her husband and Allahعَزّوجَلّ heard that conversation.

41
00:05:38,805 --> 00:05:42,736
Khawlah(خوله) was giving Umar Ibn Al-Khattab رضي الله عنه a Naseeha(نصيحه)

42
00:05:44,272 --> 00:05:47,532
and Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) was listening to it, attentively

43
00:05:48,894 --> 00:05:51,736
and she was reminding him of his humble origins.

44
00:05:58,657 --> 00:06:01,612
Al-Khansa(الخنصه), one of the woman of Al-Ansaar(الانصار),

45
00:06:05,181 --> 00:06:11,589
four of her sons were killed in the Battle of Al-Yarmook(اليرموك), four.

46
00:06:13,468 --> 00:06:16,637
When Umar Ibn Al-Khattabرضي الله عنه heard the news

47
00:06:17,617 --> 00:06:27,739
he ordered the treasurer to carry on paying their salaries to their mother, all four.

48
00:06:29,652 --> 00:06:32,625
As a reward to this patient woman,

49
00:06:33,441 --> 00:06:38,983
who was the reason behind the Shahadah(شهادة) of her sons

50
00:06:39,269 --> 00:06:43,039
because of her encouragement for them and the way she brought them up.

51
00:06:44,634 --> 00:06:49,427
She was a poetess and her poetry was so, encouraging

52
00:06:50,861 --> 00:06:54,332
and that was not only encouraging for her sons

53
00:06:54,356 --> 00:06:56,687
but it was also encouraging for all other Muslims.

54
00:07:03,119 --> 00:07:05,343
Once Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) is walking in Madina,

55
00:07:08,611 --> 00:07:12,917
so a young woman came to him - (اِمْرَأةْ شَاْبَةْ), a Woman in her youthful years.

56
00:07:15,074 --> 00:07:18,750
She came to Umar(عُمَر) and she said: O Ameer-Ul-Mo’mineen(امير المؤمنين)!

57
00:07:20,197 --> 00:07:25,549
My husband died and he left behind young children

58
00:07:27,670 --> 00:07:37,098
and he left us no land and he left us no cattle and he left us with nothing.

59
00:07:39,485 --> 00:07:44,649
And my father is Imam Ar-Rukhsa Al-Ghaffari(امام الرخصه الغفاري),

60
00:07:45,787 --> 00:07:48,981
who witnessed Sulha-Al-Hadaybiyyah(صلح حديبيه) with Rasool Allah ﷺ.

61
00:07:51,302 --> 00:07:52,835
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) said: Welcome,

62
00:07:55,414 --> 00:07:59,431
her father was Imam(اِمَام) of his people Ghifaar(غفار).

63
00:07:59,588 --> 00:08:02,849
The people of Abu Dhar(ابو زر), her father was their Imam(اِمَام).

64
00:08:05,387 --> 00:08:11,217
So, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) when he heard that she is the daughter of this man,

65
00:08:11,559 --> 00:08:15,662
this Sahabi(صحابي) of Rasool Allah ﷺ he said: Welcome, come with me.

66
00:08:17,332 --> 00:08:20,407
So, this young lady goes with Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب),

67
00:08:21,192 --> 00:08:30,488
- so he finds a very strong camel, strong back, good for carrying and he loads two huge sacks,

68
00:08:31,416 --> 00:08:37,902
he fills them up with money, food and clothes and he packs on the top of this camel

69
00:08:38,690 --> 00:08:41,221
and he handles the bridle to this woman

70
00:08:41,737 --> 00:08:46,081
and he says; Take the camel and everything on top of it, it's all yours.

71
00:08:47,654 --> 00:08:52,503
And then he told her, by the time this runs out,

72
00:08:52,888 --> 00:08:55,552
Allahعَزّوجَلّ would have provided for you with something.

73
00:08:57,914 --> 00:08:59,790
So, the man who was with Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) said;

74
00:08:59,814 --> 00:09:02,293
O Ameer-Ul-Mo’mineen(امير المؤمنين)! You have given her too much.

75
00:09:03,989 --> 00:09:08,466
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said: May your mother be bereaved of you!

76
00:09:10,550 --> 00:09:14,497
I can still remember her father and her brother

77
00:09:15,011 --> 00:09:17,855
fighting next to a fortress until, they opened it

78
00:09:18,502 --> 00:09:21,278
and now we are enjoying the fruits of their deeds.

79
00:09:22,511 --> 00:09:27,251
These men died Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله), these men died, so that we can live!

80
00:09:28,275 --> 00:09:31,473
We are now enjoying now the blessings of their efforts.

81
00:09:32,543 --> 00:09:34,902
What is in Bait-Ul-Maal(بيت المال), what is in treasury

82
00:09:34,927 --> 00:09:37,590
is because of the efforts of these Sahabah(صحابه), who fought for this Deen(دِيْن)

83
00:09:38,872 --> 00:09:44,132
and now you are telling me, that it's too much to give this woman what I gave her?

84
00:09:45,863 --> 00:09:49,807
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) would take care of the families of the Shuhada(شهداء).

85
00:09:51,064 --> 00:09:53,711
He was grateful towards the ones,

86
00:09:53,735 --> 00:10:00,262
who gave their lives for the religion of Allahعَزّوجَلّ because Rasool Allah ﷺ says;

87
00:10:01,821 --> 00:10:08,612
مَنْ جهَّزَ غَازِيًا في سبيلِ اللَّهِ فَقَدْ غَزَا، ومنْ خَلَفَ غَازيًا في أَهْلِهِ بخَيْر فَقَدْ غزَا

88
00:10:09,609 --> 00:10:14,003
The one, who finances a fighter has fought,

89
00:10:14,844 --> 00:10:19,170
and the one, who takes care of the family of the fighter has fought.

90
00:10:20,303 --> 00:10:23,579
You get the same Ajr(أجْر) if you take care of their families.

91
00:10:23,903 --> 00:10:26,571
So, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) is receiving the Ajr(أجْر) of Ghazo(غزو)

92
00:10:27,614 --> 00:10:32,349
even though he is sitting in Madina because he was taking care of the needs of these families.

93
00:10:34,261 --> 00:10:37,721
And that was the expected thing to do, that was the right thing to do.

94
00:10:41,298 --> 00:10:42,571
So, in those days,

95
00:10:43,306 --> 00:10:47,304
the Mujahid(مجاهد) Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله) would go out and he is satisfied.

96
00:10:47,329 --> 00:10:55,311
He has tranquility in his heart because he knows that his family would have something to fall back on

97
00:10:55,748 --> 00:10:57,641
 and they will have somebody to take care of them.

98
00:10:59,860 --> 00:11:01,679
But today things are very different.

99
00:11:03,048 --> 00:11:05,516
So, the ones that are Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله) today

100
00:11:06,226 --> 00:11:07,818
may Allahعَزّوجَلّ reward them and help them

101
00:11:07,842 --> 00:11:10,543
 because the days are now different, the times are different.

102
00:11:12,387 --> 00:11:16,156
One brother was telling me about a sister in Yemen.

103
00:11:17,106 --> 00:11:19,617
He is telling me about the actual situation.

104
00:11:20,957 --> 00:11:24,602
He said: He knows a wife of a Shaheed(شهيد),

105
00:11:25,958 --> 00:11:29,673
who had to go around the houses of the neighborhood,

106
00:11:30,200 --> 00:11:35,546
knocking on their doors begging for second hand clothes.

107
00:11:36,582 --> 00:11:39,811
So, that she could put on her children for the day of Eid.

108
00:11:43,143 --> 00:11:46,090
Imagine sister, if you would be in that situation

109
00:11:46,588 --> 00:11:52,591
and you have to go around begging not for new clothes but for second hand clothes,

110
00:11:53,219 --> 00:11:55,215
to put on your little ones for Eid.

111
00:11:57,820 --> 00:12:03,170
And why are you doing that because your husband did not die for himself but he died for the Ummah(امة).

112
00:12:04,178 --> 00:12:07,877
Wallah(والله) Brothers and Sisters, that’s the ultimate level of betrayal

113
00:12:08,412 --> 00:12:10,147
that we allow this to happen today.

114
00:12:12,232 --> 00:12:17,154
We have forsaken our brothers, the Ummah(امة) has forsaken them

115
00:12:17,778 --> 00:12:20,257
because they died Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله) for the sake of Ummah(امة).

116
00:12:20,281 --> 00:12:23,093
Why are they doing that? They are not doing that for their own benefits.

117
00:12:24,262 --> 00:12:28,098
This person could otherwise be a successful doctor, or engineer or business man,

118
00:12:28,434 --> 00:12:30,914
he could be making living for himself and family

119
00:12:31,442 --> 00:12:35,777
but he went out for the sake of YOU and then this is how he is treated.

120
00:12:37,192 --> 00:12:41,312
He is betrayed, his wife is betrayed, their children are betrayed

121
00:12:41,561 --> 00:12:45,048
and not only that people will go on the media talking against him.

122
00:12:45,073 --> 00:12:49,887
Muslims are going to go on Media talking against him.

123
00:12:50,498 --> 00:12:52,790
when he has given his life for the sake of Ummah(امة).

124
00:12:55,632 --> 00:12:59,081
Nothing goes for free, we will be held accountable for that on the day of judgment.

125
00:13:00,335 --> 00:13:04,393
You will be held accountable for what is happening today, if you don’t do a thing about it.

126
00:13:05,789 --> 00:13:09,440
And when you see your brothers wherever they are, being harassed,

127
00:13:10,672 --> 00:13:15,279
being arrested, being abused, and you do nothing about it

128
00:13:16,024 --> 00:13:18,762
beware and realize that you will be next

129
00:13:19,718 --> 00:13:22,853
and in addition to paying for that sin in Duniyah(دُنِيَّا)

130
00:13:22,999 --> 00:13:26,308
Allahعَزّوجَلّ will make you pay hefty price on the day of judgment.

131
00:13:27,943 --> 00:13:30,408
If you allow this to happen to your brothers,

132
00:13:31,670 --> 00:13:34,632
be assured that the punishment is on its way.

133
00:13:36,559 --> 00:13:41,071
It will happen in your health, or in your family or in your wealth.

134
00:13:41,418 --> 00:13:44,062
Allahعَزّوجَلّ is going to make you pay for that.

135
00:13:45,268 --> 00:13:47,044
Why? Because we are an Ummah(امة)

136
00:13:47,434 --> 00:13:54,442
and this membership is not a free membership that is giving to you without any duties.

137
00:13:55,461 --> 00:13:57,888
Being a member of the Ummah(امة) of Muhammadﷺ

138
00:13:57,912 --> 00:14:00,791
carries with it, responsibility because it's an honor.

139
00:14:01,687 --> 00:14:04,128
It is such a great honor that Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء)

140
00:14:05,654 --> 00:14:09,158
would wish to be member of Ummah(امة) of Muhammadﷺ.

141
00:14:09,896 --> 00:14:15,172
Musa عليه السلام he would wish to be a member of Ummah(امة) of Muhammadﷺ

142
00:14:15,203 --> 00:14:20,476
and Allahعَزّوجَلّ has gave you that virtue, Allahعَزّوجَلّ gave you that honor

143
00:14:20,859 --> 00:14:23,941
to make you part of greatest Ummah(امة) that ever existed,

144
00:14:23,965 --> 00:14:25,916
كُنْتُمْ خَيْرَ أُمَّةٍ أُخْرِجَتْ لِلنَّاسِ

145
00:14:27,817 --> 00:14:29,484
But that honor is not free

146
00:14:29,898 --> 00:14:32,969
there are some duties and responsibilities that are tied to it.

147
00:14:33,776 --> 00:14:35,303
And those duties are

148
00:14:35,501 --> 00:14:41,756
that you are responsible towards the welfare of every member of this Ummah(امة).

149
00:14:42,159 --> 00:14:47,307
And if there is something that you could do to help a brother or sister, who is in need,

150
00:14:47,502 --> 00:14:49,244
and then you do nothing about it,

151
00:14:50,003 --> 00:14:53,308
be assured that Allahعَزّوجَلّ will hold you accountable for that.

152
00:14:53,625 --> 00:14:56,394
Because Rasool Allah ﷺ said: this Ummah(امة) is like a body,

153
00:14:56,507 --> 00:15:02,586
if one part of it feels a pain, the whole body joins in the pain and fever and suffering.

154
00:15:03,933 --> 00:15:07,324
You cannot separate your finger from rest of the body.

155
00:15:08,470 --> 00:15:13,597
Even if that small finger is injured the whole body will feel the pain.

156
00:15:28,498 --> 00:15:33,105
With other family issues Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) would also deal with them.

157
00:15:33,992 --> 00:15:41,773
For example, a man said, I want to divorce my wife.

158
00:15:43,368 --> 00:15:44,423
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) said;

159
00:15:44,659 --> 00:15:45,701
وَلِمَا تُطَلِّقُهَا؟

160
00:15:45,725 --> 00:15:47,522
Why do you want to divorce her?

161
00:15:48,736 --> 00:15:50,086
 He said: Because I don’t love her.

162
00:15:52,116 --> 00:15:53,570
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) said;

163
00:15:55,546 --> 00:15:59,151
اَوَ كُلْ اَلْبُيُوْتَ بُنِيَتَ عَلَى الْحُبَّ؟

164
00:16:00,882 --> 00:16:05,182
And since when have all the houses been established on love?

165
00:16:06,808 --> 00:16:07,742
فَاَيْنَ رِّعَائِيَةْ ؟

166
00:16:07,766 --> 00:16:08,719
Where is the care?

167
00:16:10,246 --> 00:16:19,666
What Umar(عُمَر) is saying رضي الله عنه is that not every husband and wife love each other

168
00:16:20,459 --> 00:16:23,167
and that’s not the sole purpose of marriage.

169
00:16:25,587 --> 00:16:30,797
He is saying there are many families that are established on other reasons,

170
00:16:30,822 --> 00:16:37,999
yes may be they use to love each other before but hearts can change, things can go wrong,

171
00:16:39,015 --> 00:16:41,335
does that mean that family now should separate,

172
00:16:41,445 --> 00:16:43,429
just because you don’t love your wife anymore,

173
00:16:43,686 --> 00:16:44,334
"فَاَيْنَ رِّعَائِيَةْ ؟"

174
00:16:44,450 --> 00:16:45,050
 Where is care?

175
00:16:47,361 --> 00:16:50,287
Allahعَزّوجَلّ put between male and female

176
00:16:53,103 --> 00:16:54,178
مُوَّدَّةْ وَ رَحْمَةَ

177
00:16:55,118 --> 00:16:58,134
Muwaddah(مودة) is love and Rahmah(رحمه) is mercy.

178
00:16:58,159 --> 00:17:03,633
If there is no love there still should be mercy, there is care, there is compassion.

179
00:17:05,855 --> 00:17:08,278
A husband should still take care of his wife,

180
00:17:08,302 --> 00:17:10,647
even though he might not love her and vice versa.

181
00:17:13,216 --> 00:17:16,286
And for Muslims who are living for the sake of Akhirah(آخرة)

182
00:17:16,755 --> 00:17:22,192
a family is a nucleus to build, to raise up children.

183
00:17:22,882 --> 00:17:26,463
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) and Allah Ho Alam(الله اعلم), we might get into that later on.

184
00:17:26,944 --> 00:17:30,868
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said: Sometime I force myself to sleep with my wife

185
00:17:31,159 --> 00:17:33,276
even though I don’t want to.

186
00:17:33,506 --> 00:17:38,809
 He doesn’t feel that desire at that moment but he would force himself to sleep with his wife.

187
00:17:39,246 --> 00:17:41,812
Why? So that may be Allahعَزّوجَلّ produce,

188
00:17:41,836 --> 00:17:43,308
نَثَّمَا تُسَّبِحُ الله

189
00:17:43,820 --> 00:17:49,520
Because may be out of that Allahعَزّوجَلّ will create a soul, "that will glorify Allah".

190
00:17:51,818 --> 00:17:55,832
So, there are other objectives that the religion would be carried on

191
00:17:55,857 --> 00:17:58,115
 that there will be people who will raise this religion

192
00:17:58,140 --> 00:18:01,632
and protect it and fight for it, and worship Allahعَزّوجَلّ.

193
00:18:02,967 --> 00:18:05,502
So, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) was telling the man hold on to your wife.

194
00:18:10,299 --> 00:18:17,581
Romance is not everything and sometimes, it could be elusive.

195
00:18:19,216 --> 00:18:25,459
You know in the beginning they are day dreaming Twenty-Four-Seven(24/7) about each other.

196
00:18:26,044 --> 00:18:31,962
But then when they get married, you know, things get, you start taking things for granted.

197
00:18:31,986 --> 00:18:38,864
When you have something you don’t really have that attachment to it, as when it's not in your hand.

198
00:18:40,086 --> 00:18:45,075
And then problem happens, and each problem might leave behind a scar,

199
00:18:46,703 --> 00:18:50,280
so you have dents and scars in heart that keep on accumulating

200
00:18:50,304 --> 00:18:53,037
and eventually may be hearts change.

201
00:18:53,394 --> 00:18:54,433
That happens a lot.

202
00:18:54,973 --> 00:18:56,285
That happens a lot.

203
00:18:57,511 --> 00:19:00,128
But the Ma’roof(معروف) should remain.

204
00:19:01,140 --> 00:19:03,894
The good treatment should remain, the mercy should remain.

205
00:19:04,249 --> 00:19:13,012
Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله) since, the female was created from the male

206
00:19:15,384 --> 00:19:25,382
each one fulfills something in the soul of the other.

207
00:19:26,240 --> 00:19:28,981
You see Hawwa(حوّا) wasn’t created independently.

208
00:19:29,724 --> 00:19:31,708
She was created out of the rib of Adam(آدم).

209
00:19:32,787 --> 00:19:34,896
So, she was created from him.

210
00:19:36,938 --> 00:19:39,629
And that is why Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله) you would find that this relationship

211
00:19:39,654 --> 00:19:43,133
between husband and wife is special and unique relationship.

212
00:19:43,799 --> 00:19:45,669
There is no relationship similar to it.

213
00:19:46,106 --> 00:19:48,205
The relationship that you have with your friends is different,

214
00:19:48,230 --> 00:19:50,367
with your parents is different, with your children is different.

215
00:19:50,762 --> 00:19:55,371
This relationship between husband and wife is different, it is unique.

216
00:19:56,452 --> 00:20:00,651
Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله) nothing seems to be able to exist independently.

217
00:20:01,515 --> 00:20:03,720
Allah has created everything in pairs.

218
00:20:04,765 --> 00:20:10,489
سُبْحَانَ الَّذِي خَلَقَ الْأَزْوَاجَ كُلَّهَا مِمَّا تُنبِتُ الْأَرْضُ وَمِنْ أَنفُسِهِمْ وَمِمَّا لَا يَعْلَمُونَ۝

219
00:20:11,415 --> 00:20:15,932
Glory be to, He, Who created things in pairs, He created you in pairs

220
00:20:16,329 --> 00:20:20,828
and created plants in pairs and created things that you don’t know in pairs.

221
00:20:21,152 --> 00:20:24,708
Only Allahعَزّوجَلّ is independent and doesn’t need a partner.

222
00:20:27,464 --> 00:20:30,291
Allah(الله) is Al-Fard As-Samad(فَرْدَا الصَّمَدْ), He doesn’t need a partner

223
00:20:31,514 --> 00:20:37,146
but this is reflection of our human deficiency that we need a pair, we need spouse,

224
00:20:38,529 --> 00:20:40,624
it's part of your Deen(دِيْن),

225
00:20:41,122 --> 00:20:43,852
because it's part of your humanity, it's part of your human make up.

226
00:20:44,388 --> 00:20:49,567
You are deficient until, that missing piece of the puzzle comes into your life.

227
00:20:51,368 --> 00:21:00,109
And this need even exist when there is no love between the couple, that is still needed.

228
00:21:17,789 --> 00:21:23,100
Similarly, this time a woman came, complaining about her husband.

229
00:21:24,765 --> 00:21:30,474
She came to Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) and she said about her husband;

230
00:21:31,371 --> 00:21:34,411
قَلَّا خَيْرُه’ وَ كَثُرَ شَرُّهُُ

231
00:21:36,973 --> 00:21:39,812
"His good is little and his evil is a lot".

232
00:21:40,571 --> 00:21:48,872
The good that comes from my husband is little and the evil that comes from him, is a lot.

233
00:21:49,689 --> 00:21:51,323
He said: Who is your husband?

234
00:21:51,640 --> 00:21:52,966
She said, Abu Salamah(ابو سلمه).

235
00:21:54,181 --> 00:21:56,166
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) asked the ones with him, he said,

236
00:21:56,190 --> 00:22:00,774
all we know about Abu Salamah(ابو سلمه) is, he a very nice man.

237
00:22:00,868 --> 00:22:02,552
He is one of the Sahaba رضي الله عنهم.

238
00:22:03,431 --> 00:22:06,710
So, Umar(عُمَر) was kind of shocked to hear this statement by his wife.

239
00:22:08,075 --> 00:22:09,946
So, he said: Bring the husband in.

240
00:22:09,986 --> 00:22:11,166
So, they brought the husband, he said:

241
00:22:11,206 --> 00:22:13,037
Do you know this woman he said: Yes, my wife.

242
00:22:13,307 --> 00:22:14,205
What is she saying?

243
00:22:14,677 --> 00:22:19,738
He said: She claims that your good is very little and your evil is a lot.

244
00:22:20,867 --> 00:22:21,858
He said: She is lying.

245
00:22:25,320 --> 00:22:29,722
I am treating her in the best way a husband could treat his wife

246
00:22:29,903 --> 00:22:33,203
and I am providing for her very well but

247
00:22:33,332 --> 00:22:34,504
اَنَا رَجُلٌ بَقِيْ

248
00:22:35,176 --> 00:22:43,513
He was old, and Baqi(بقي) means a camel or a goat that is running out of milk.

249
00:22:44,968 --> 00:22:50,122
He was figuratively speaking to refer to impotence.

250
00:22:50,900 --> 00:22:57,092
He was becoming impotent, and that’s why his wife was complaining.

251
00:22:59,139 --> 00:23:00,664
So, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) said;

252
00:23:01,077 --> 00:23:02,132
يَا عَدُّوَتْ نَفْسَهَا

253
00:23:02,156 --> 00:23:05,115
O you enemy of yourself! He was carrying his stick obviously.

254
00:23:07,174 --> 00:23:19,214
He said: You consumed his youthful years and you lived off his wealth,

255
00:23:20,046 --> 00:23:24,548
and now when he becomes old, you come and complain about him?

256
00:23:24,603 --> 00:23:26,243
And lie against him.

257
00:23:28,684 --> 00:23:32,475
She said: O Ameer-Ul-Mo’mineen(امير المؤمنين)! I am sorry you're never going to see me here again.

258
00:23:35,189 --> 00:23:41,738
Even though Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) was delivering this harsh statement to her, he still gave her a gift.

259
00:23:41,858 --> 00:23:44,677
 He gave her Thalatha Al-Thwab(ثلاثة الاثواب) three pieces of cloth.

260
00:23:45,301 --> 00:23:48,117
So, the narrator said: I saw her grabbing them and run away.

261
00:23:50,027 --> 00:23:55,760
And then he told her:

262
00:23:55,850 --> 00:23:57,604
اَحْسَنِيْ صُحْبَتْ هَذَا الشَّيْخ

263
00:23:59,389 --> 00:24:01,989
Be good company of this old man.

264
00:24:03,134 --> 00:24:05,929
Be of good company of this old man.

265
00:24:06,696 --> 00:24:09,289
And then when she Left, he came to the husband and said;

266
00:24:09,509 --> 00:24:14,780
Don’t think because I gave her those stern words that I am going to let you off the hook.

267
00:24:15,683 --> 00:24:22,928
You have to be good with your wife and then he left.

268
00:24:23,394 --> 00:24:29,811
So, over here, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) did not see valid ground for this woman to complain about the husband,

269
00:24:30,360 --> 00:24:34,790
if it was a problem that came up early on in the marriage when they were still young

270
00:24:34,815 --> 00:24:41,356
and the husband was unable to fulfill these natural needs of his wife

271
00:24:41,918 --> 00:24:44,008
then those would be grounds for divorce.

272
00:24:45,169 --> 00:24:47,437
But that's not how the man was, when he man was young.

273
00:24:47,726 --> 00:24:50,026
This was the problem that came him when he was old.

274
00:24:50,702 --> 00:24:53,376
So, Umar(عُمَر) told the woman you spent all of these years with him

275
00:24:53,400 --> 00:24:56,987
and now, when he is old, you want to desert him and leave him.

276
00:25:04,018 --> 00:25:08,634
Hind Bint Ut'bah(هند بنت عتبعه) was known as

277
00:25:08,939 --> 00:25:12,455
being very intelligent and beautiful woman in Quraish(قُرَيْشْ).

278
00:25:13,121 --> 00:25:15,984
She was initially married to the uncle of Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد)

279
00:25:16,566 --> 00:25:19,402
but then he divorced her and she married Abu Sufiyan(ابوسفيان).

280
00:25:19,738 --> 00:25:22,839
And she stayed with him for the majority of her life

281
00:25:23,090 --> 00:25:25,887
but then eventually Abu Sufiyan(ابوسفيان) divorced her.

282
00:25:27,758 --> 00:25:32,769
So, she went to Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) and she borrowed money from him.

283
00:25:33,883 --> 00:25:38,663
Because since she's on her own, she wanted to do some business.

284
00:25:39,487 --> 00:25:42,025
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) agreed and he gave her some money,

285
00:25:42,056 --> 00:25:46,766
so she went to Iraq and she started investing

286
00:25:46,821 --> 00:25:51,584
 and she became very successful in running her business.

287
00:25:52,317 --> 00:25:54,604
And the reason that why I am bringing this up, is to show you that

288
00:25:54,628 --> 00:26:00,494
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) would take care the needs of these women  in their young age, in their old age.

289
00:26:00,640 --> 00:26:04,481
He gave her the money from the treasury in order to invest

290
00:26:05,296 --> 00:26:10,754
and that was something that was accommodated by the Muslims in those days.

291
00:26:10,786 --> 00:26:13,445
Woman could go and trade and do business and make money

292
00:26:13,981 --> 00:26:16,406
and that’s what Hind Bint Ut'bah(هند بنت عتبعه) did.

293
00:26:17,478 --> 00:26:18,858
To sum it up.

294
00:26:20,043 --> 00:26:22,732
I think this statement tells it all.

295
00:26:23,311 --> 00:26:25,693
It shows you the concern that Umar(عُمَر) had for women.

296
00:26:25,795 --> 00:26:28,844
You know some of the statements that were previously mentioned

297
00:26:29,022 --> 00:26:32,352
might give you an impression that Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) was harsh on women

298
00:26:32,432 --> 00:26:34,707
 that's not true that’s furthest from the truth.

299
00:26:35,042 --> 00:26:39,332
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) did not want women intervening in his business.

300
00:26:40,336 --> 00:26:44,421
But he was very soft hearted and kind when it came to women.

301
00:26:46,560 --> 00:26:53,294
He was their protector, he was their leader, he was their caretaker.

302
00:26:54,587 --> 00:26:56,575
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab رضي الله عنه said;

303
00:26:58,071 --> 00:27:06,304
وَاللهِ لَا اِنْ سَلَّمَنِيَّ الله لَا اَدَعَنَّ اَرَامِ لَا اَهْلِ الّاعراق لَا يَحْتَجْنَ اِلَى اَحَدٍ بَعْدِيْ

304
00:27:07,996 --> 00:27:12,015
He said: In the name of Allah, if Allah gives me life,

305
00:27:13,121 --> 00:27:21,177
I am not going to allow any of the widows of Iraq, in need of the help of anyone after me.

306
00:27:22,990 --> 00:27:24,728
If Allah just grants me life,

307
00:27:25,693 --> 00:27:29,666
I am going to make the women of Iraq and that was the farthest part of his Empire.

308
00:27:29,896 --> 00:27:32,335
I am going to make the women of Iraq, the widows,

309
00:27:33,287 --> 00:27:36,631
I am going to make them so content, and happy, and pleased

310
00:27:37,362 --> 00:27:40,710
that, they are not going to need the help of anyone who comes after me.

311
00:27:43,229 --> 00:27:48,184
That is how he viewed his responsibility towards the women of the Khilafah(خِلَافَه).

312
00:27:56,285 --> 00:28:06,636
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab رضي الله عنه, one day he was on a camel and it was very hot.

313
00:28:08,045 --> 00:28:12,909
It was noon time in Madina very hot and he is running on the top of his camel

314
00:28:13,022 --> 00:28:17,663
in the hot sun, sand blowing in his face.

315
00:28:19,324 --> 00:28:23,286
Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) said: Ameer-Ul-Mo’mineen(امير المؤمنين) where are you heading?

316
00:28:23,785 --> 00:28:27,681
He said: A camel of a Sadaqah(صدقه) ran away and I am pursuing it.

317
00:28:28,881 --> 00:28:32,262
This was something that a slave could do, a servant could do,

318
00:28:33,584 --> 00:28:34,731
Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) said;

319
00:28:34,762 --> 00:28:36,900
لَقَدْ اَطَعَّبْتَ مَنْ جَاءَ بَعْدَكْ

320
00:28:37,311 --> 00:28:40,036
You are making it difficult on anyone, who will come after you.

321
00:28:41,860 --> 00:28:45,363
The standard that you are setting for the Khilafah(خِلَافَه) is so high,

322
00:28:45,907 --> 00:28:48,578
you are making it difficult on all of the Khulafah(خلافاء) after you.

323
00:28:50,349 --> 00:28:52,248
He was setting the bar so high.

324
00:28:53,646 --> 00:28:57,420
Ali(علي) was worried about whoever will assume this responsibilty after Umar(عُمَر)

325
00:28:57,460 --> 00:29:03,693
will he be able to live up, to the standards set by Umar Ibn Al-Khattab رضي الله عنه .

326
00:29:08,486 --> 00:29:13,885
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب), he would give the right assessment of people

327
00:29:13,965 --> 00:29:17,178
 and he would honor the people that deserved to be honored and

328
00:29:20,127 --> 00:29:21,878
يُنْزِلَ االنَّاسْ مَنَازِلَهُمْ

329
00:29:22,789 --> 00:29:24,847
He would put the people in the right level,

330
00:29:28,312 --> 00:29:30,551
and he was careful in his judgments of others.

331
00:29:31,251 --> 00:29:37,555
Once he needed somebody to give reference to someone, "Shahadah(شهادة)"

332
00:29:39,883 --> 00:29:42,432
so, someone said, I will give him reference

333
00:29:43,641 --> 00:29:45,574
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said: Based on what?

334
00:29:46,043 --> 00:29:47,259
Are you his neighbor?

335
00:29:47,783 --> 00:29:48,846
He said: No,

336
00:29:50,026 --> 00:29:51,596
He said: Did you live with him?

337
00:29:52,140 --> 00:29:53,187
 He said: No,

338
00:29:54,221 --> 00:29:55,829
He said: Did you do business with him?

339
00:29:56,337 --> 00:29:57,337
He said: No,

340
00:29:57,816 --> 00:29:59,516
He said: Did you travel with him?

341
00:30:00,627 --> 00:30:02,121
فَاِنَّهُمْ مَحَقِّ الرِّجَالْ

342
00:30:02,350 --> 00:30:06,262
Because travelling is the test, is the real test of men.

343
00:30:07,310 --> 00:30:08,221
 He said: No,

344
00:30:08,560 --> 00:30:09,726
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) said;

345
00:30:09,982 --> 00:30:12,704
لَعَلَّكَ الرَاَيْتَه’ يُصَلِّيْ قَائِمًا وَ قَاعِدَةْ

346
00:30:13,115 --> 00:30:16,232
Well may be you then met him in the Masjid(مسجد) and you saw him praying,

347
00:30:18,216 --> 00:30:19,199
He said: Yes,

348
00:30:19,495 --> 00:30:21,872
He said: Go! because you don’t really know him.

349
00:30:24,101 --> 00:30:28,364
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said: You don’t judge the person based on seeing him in the Masjid(مسجد).

350
00:30:32,801 --> 00:30:34,159
Are you his neighbor?

351
00:30:36,484 --> 00:30:38,871
Did you live with him, Were you his room-mate?

352
00:30:39,551 --> 00:30:42,864
That's how you get to know people, did you do business with him?

353
00:30:43,345 --> 00:30:49,966
When money comes in you know a certain aspect of the personality of the person.

354
00:30:50,727 --> 00:30:55,705
A person could be a sweet tongue, they could be a wonderful brothers,

355
00:30:55,980 --> 00:30:59,641
but when it comes to money the dark side comes out.

356
00:31:01,417 --> 00:31:02,945
And then he said: Did you travelled with him?.

357
00:31:03,627 --> 00:31:07,483
فَاِنَّ اسَفَرْ وَالْاِغْتٍرَابْ مَحَقِّ الرِجَالْ

358
00:31:08,057 --> 00:31:09,752
That’s the true test of men.

359
00:31:10,721 --> 00:31:17,211
When you travel, when you leave behind routine of your life, the comforts of your life,

360
00:31:18,541 --> 00:31:25,809
things start getting on your nerves and the real you comes out.

361
00:31:27,078 --> 00:31:31,474
Your sleep schedule changes, you are sleeping on a different bed,

362
00:31:31,884 --> 00:31:35,611
you are eating different food, you know you are used to food of your mom

363
00:31:35,658 --> 00:31:40,039
now you are eating the food of someone else different country.

364
00:31:41,155 --> 00:31:43,084
There's not enough spices in the food,

365
00:31:46,949 --> 00:31:52,374
the routine changes and you are always close to your travel companions

366
00:31:53,539 --> 00:31:57,166
this is how Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) assesses people.

367
00:31:58,148 --> 00:32:01,838
So, he said, you are not qualified to give him a reference.

368
00:32:09,220 --> 00:32:10,538
And he has some other statements,

369
00:32:10,578 --> 00:32:17,109
he said: I am not really worried about the Mo’min(مؤمن)

370
00:32:17,177 --> 00:32:20,690
whose Eeman(ايمان) is clear and the Kafir(كافر) whose Kuffr(كفر) is clear

371
00:32:21,155 --> 00:32:27,147
but I am worried about the Munafiq(منافق), who shows Eeman(ايمان) and conceals Kuffr(كفر).

372
00:32:29,183 --> 00:32:30,629
And he has some statements about,

373
00:32:32,448 --> 00:32:36,611
Don’t be fooled by the worship that you see of people,

374
00:32:40,412 --> 00:32:45,148
because what is in their hearts could be different and all of these statements are true.

375
00:32:46,724 --> 00:32:52,781
It's not the Salah(صلاة) of the person, it's not the ibadah(عبادة) that, they show to others,

376
00:32:53,617 --> 00:32:57,410
there could be some diseases of heart that are still lingering behind

377
00:32:58,227 --> 00:33:00,129
and you don’t really see them but Allah sees them.

378
00:33:02,979 --> 00:33:09,399
Some of the first people turned down the Daw'ah(دعوة) of Eesaعليه السلام were the scholars of Bannu Israel(بنواسرائيل).

379
00:33:10,706 --> 00:33:15,928
They were the first the Muftees(مفتي) of the Banni Israel(بني اسرائيل), the Ulama(علماء) of Banni Israel(بني اسرائيل)

380
00:33:16,301 --> 00:33:22,418
 they were the first to turn down Eesa عليه السلام they and the Umara(امراء).

381
00:33:22,753 --> 00:33:26,622
The Umara(امراء) and the Ulama(علماء) were the first to betray Eesa عليه السلام.

382
00:33:27,213 --> 00:33:29,373
The political leaders and the religious leaders

383
00:33:29,938 --> 00:33:32,676
and the ones, who followed the Eesaعليه السلام

384
00:33:32,946 --> 00:33:40,462
were some fishermen and some simple lay men, the ignorant, simple minded people

385
00:33:41,042 --> 00:33:45,129
they were the ones whom Allah choose to follow Eesa عليه السلام and they were his Hawariyeen(حوارين).

386
00:33:46,711 --> 00:33:54,304
So, don’t be fooled by the tongue and by the appearance because only Allah can see what is inside.

387
00:33:56,017 --> 00:34:00,681
Let's all make Dua(دُعَا) "that Allahعَزّوجَلّ make the inside of us better than the outside".

388
00:34:01,448 --> 00:34:05,027
اَللَّهُمَّ اجْعَلْ سَرِيْرَتَنَا خَيْرًا مِنْ عَلى نِيَّتِنَا

389
00:34:13,372 --> 00:34:18,995
Odae bin Haatim(عديئ ابن حاتم), one of the noble men of his people, one of the Sahabah of Rasool Allah ﷺ,

390
00:34:19,463 --> 00:34:22,378
He said: I came with a delegation of my people about two thousand

391
00:34:23,056 --> 00:34:30,099
and we came to Umar(عُمَر) and he started choosing some men from my people and he would give them,

392
00:34:31,988 --> 00:34:39,848
so I stood in front of him he ignored me, he turned the other side.

393
00:34:39,873 --> 00:34:44,467
So, I went in front of him and he again ignored me and it happened few times.

394
00:34:45,914 --> 00:34:48,838
And then I went straight to him and I said: O Umar(عُمَر)! You don’t know me?

395
00:34:49,024 --> 00:34:50,036
You don’t remember me?

396
00:34:51,563 --> 00:34:57,313
Odae(عديئ) said: Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) laughed, so much that he fell on his back.

397
00:34:58,917 --> 00:35:01,050
And he said: No! Odae(عديئ) I know you very well.

398
00:35:03,519 --> 00:35:06,874
You are the one, who believed when people disbelieved,

399
00:35:07,581 --> 00:35:11,033
You are the one who came, when people deserted,

400
00:35:11,662 --> 00:35:16,599
and you are the one, who was true to his words, when people betrayed,

401
00:35:18,357 --> 00:35:21,386
and you are the one, who came with the Sadaqah(صدقه) of Tai(طيئ),

402
00:35:21,937 --> 00:35:25,730
and that was the Sadaqah(صدقه) that made Rasool Allah ﷺ and the Sahabah(صحابه) happy.

403
00:35:28,734 --> 00:35:33,412
And he apologized to me and then he said: The reason, why I am giving these men that you see

404
00:35:33,437 --> 00:35:35,851
is because these are leaders among their people

405
00:35:36,757 --> 00:35:41,099
and they are the men, whom people go to in their times of need

406
00:35:41,572 --> 00:35:43,368
and that’s why I am giving them.

407
00:35:45,276 --> 00:35:46,576
Odae bin Haatim(عديئ ابن حاتم) said;

408
00:35:48,322 --> 00:35:49,404
فَلَا اُبَالِيْ اِذَنْ

409
00:35:50,124 --> 00:35:52,168
I am happy then, if that’s the case.

410
00:35:53,428 --> 00:35:56,606
So, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب)  recognizes the status of Odae(عديئ)

411
00:35:56,724 --> 00:35:59,616
and he also recognized the status of the leaders of his people

412
00:35:59,776 --> 00:36:04,967
and the reason why he was giving them, is because through their hands others would benefit.

413
00:36:05,988 --> 00:36:08,519
He was giving them because these are the men

414
00:36:08,847 --> 00:36:11,320
whom their people come to in moments of need.

415
00:36:12,592 --> 00:36:15,072
Allahعَزّوجَلّ gives some people money

416
00:36:16,013 --> 00:36:20,962
because these wealthy men distributes that money to the needy.

417
00:36:21,731 --> 00:36:24,790
The moment the start holding back

418
00:36:25,146 --> 00:36:28,004
Allahعَزّوجَلّ will take that wealth and give it to somebody else.

419
00:36:31,552 --> 00:36:35,645
In battle with Romans some Muslims were taken as prisoners of war.

420
00:36:36,616 --> 00:36:47,789
So, the Roman King when he heard that one of them was a Sahabi(صحابي), he was so happy.

421
00:36:48,947 --> 00:36:50,677
He said: Bring me, I want to meet him.

422
00:36:51,260 --> 00:36:54,928
The Sahabah(صحابه) by now so many legends were surrounding them

423
00:36:55,052 --> 00:37:01,937
and news going around the globe about these special men, SAHABAH(صحابه) of Rasool Allah ﷺ

424
00:37:02,981 --> 00:37:05,741
so, they were just fascinated, they just wanted to see a Sahabi(صحابي).

425
00:37:06,415 --> 00:37:08,661
So, the Roman King said: Bring him to me.

426
00:37:10,227 --> 00:37:13,983
Because these Sahabah(صحابه) one counts them as an Ummah(امة).

427
00:37:14,509 --> 00:37:15,918
One man is equal to an Ummah(امة).

428
00:37:19,511 --> 00:37:22,058
That was the product that Rasool Allah ﷺ left behind.

429
00:37:23,394 --> 00:37:24,994
So, they brought Abdullah Bin Hudhafah(عبدالله ابن حدافه).

430
00:37:26,323 --> 00:37:36,673
And this Roman King is now thinking, and he's thinking about how to capitalize on the Sahabi(صحابي).

431
00:37:37,952 --> 00:37:41,277
So, he said: I want you to marry my daughter.

432
00:37:42,804 --> 00:37:49,259
Apparently he use to think, there is special about the genes of the Sahabah(صحابه).

433
00:37:50,447 --> 00:37:57,927
He wants that to be carried down the line by him, marrying him to his daughter.

434
00:37:59,792 --> 00:38:04,000
So, this is the daughter of a Roman King, she is going to marry this Sahabi(صحابي),

435
00:38:04,332 --> 00:38:06,035
their children are going to be a superman.

436
00:38:12,219 --> 00:38:16,864
But he set a condition that you became a Christian. He said: I won’t,

437
00:38:17,594 --> 00:38:24,253
he said: Listen, you marry my daughter and I will give you half of my kingdom.

438
00:38:26,308 --> 00:38:29,986
Abdullah Bin Hudhafah(عبدالله ابن حدافه) said: No way, I am not giving up my religion.

439
00:38:32,377 --> 00:38:37,832
Brothers don’t take it as a tale, think about it, Half the kingdom,

440
00:38:39,486 --> 00:38:45,820
some Muslims are selling out today for a miser salary, for peanuts.

441
00:38:46,578 --> 00:38:51,213
They are betraying the Ummah(امة), they are spying on the Muslims for nothing.

442
00:38:51,921 --> 00:38:54,316
يَبِيْعُوْنَا دِيْنَهُمْ بِعَرْضِ مِّنَّ الدُّنْيَاء قَلِيْلَ

443
00:38:54,340 --> 00:38:58,050
They are selling their religion for a very miser price for nothing.

444
00:38:58,820 --> 00:39:00,966
They are giving up Islam, they are committing Ridda(ردة)

445
00:39:03,588 --> 00:39:10,729
- and this Sahabi(صحابي) is offered half the kingdom, half of the kingdom and he says, No!

446
00:39:14,687 --> 00:39:19,041
You know when you say, no to these people how much it hurts them?

447
00:39:20,280 --> 00:39:24,914
I am offering you my daughter, I am king, nobody ever said no to me, in my life

448
00:39:26,467 --> 00:39:31,705
and I never offered my daughter to anyone in my kingdom before and you say, No?

449
00:39:32,149 --> 00:39:34,423
And then I give you half of my kingdom and you say, No?

450
00:39:34,802 --> 00:39:37,726
the people of Duniyah(دُنِيَّا) they have fought so much to get the Duniyah(دُنِيَّا)

451
00:39:38,006 --> 00:39:41,163
when they see someone, who is not attached to Duniyah(دُنِيَّا), it drives them crazy.

452
00:39:46,313 --> 00:39:48,337
It is as if you are insulting me and telling me that

453
00:39:48,361 --> 00:39:51,173
I wasted my life for something that is wrong.

454
00:39:51,258 --> 00:39:53,932
As if you are telling me that this Duniyah(دُنِيَّا) is not worth it.

455
00:39:54,241 --> 00:39:55,025
 What do you mean?

456
00:39:55,169 --> 00:39:59,515
You are refusing half of my kingdom, I am offering you my daughter and you say, No.

457
00:40:00,380 --> 00:40:03,766
So it just drive him crazy, it makes him angry.

458
00:40:06,120 --> 00:40:09,577
So, he said: Bring the Al-Bakara(البكرة),

459
00:40:09,601 --> 00:40:18,992
Al-Bakara(البكرة) is apparently this huge container, bowl, that looks like a cow.

460
00:40:19,906 --> 00:40:24,473
And it is used for burning alive.

461
00:40:24,970 --> 00:40:30,372
They would fill it with oil and they would just set fire to it and the oil would boil.

462
00:40:30,634 --> 00:40:33,798
Imagine that oil, with smokes coming out of it.

463
00:40:34,599 --> 00:40:39,232
Because they set it on fire for so long that it was boiling.

464
00:40:40,693 --> 00:40:44,797
And then they bring a Muslim and they throw him in that boiling oil.

465
00:40:46,401 --> 00:40:47,441
The narrator said;

466
00:40:49,766 --> 00:40:57,147
"It wasn’t very long after that Muslim was thrown in the boiling water that his bones started to sticking out."

467
00:40:58,437 --> 00:41:03,146
It is so hot that his flesh was fried, the bones came out.

468
00:41:03,557 --> 00:41:07,917
You know when you fry, if you take for an example a chicken and you fry it,

469
00:41:09,361 --> 00:41:14,352
the bones sticks out because the flesh shrinks.

470
00:41:15,848 --> 00:41:20,414
It loses all of the water vapor in it, and it shrinks, so the bones sticks out.

471
00:41:22,231 --> 00:41:25,387
That is what happened to this Muslim prisoner of war

472
00:41:26,024 --> 00:41:29,090
and that was occurring in front of the eyes of Abdullah Bin Hudhafah(عبدالله ابن حدافه).

473
00:41:30,328 --> 00:41:33,693
So, the king told him: Are you going to give up your religion now?

474
00:41:35,897 --> 00:41:39,108
Otherwise we are going to throw you in that boiling oil.

475
00:41:39,145 --> 00:41:40,589
He said: I am not going to give up my religion.

476
00:41:44,257 --> 00:41:46,690
So, they said throw him in that oil.

477
00:41:47,551 --> 00:41:48,471
They picked him up,

478
00:41:50,757 --> 00:41:51,846
Abdullah(عبدالله) started to cry.

479
00:41:54,784 --> 00:41:57,146
They went to the king and said: He is crying.

480
00:41:57,170 --> 00:41:58,500
The king said: Bring him back.

481
00:42:00,260 --> 00:42:01,699
He is crying and he has weakened,

482
00:42:02,120 --> 00:42:07,256
he has weakened we got him, we struck fear in his heart.

483
00:42:08,605 --> 00:42:09,305
Bring him to me

484
00:42:10,178 --> 00:42:12,548
He said, alright. Are you ready to give up your religion?

485
00:42:14,264 --> 00:42:18,620
Abdullah(عبدالله) said: Don’t think that I cried because of fear of death

486
00:42:21,384 --> 00:42:26,407
but the reason I cried, is because I remembered, that I only have one soul

487
00:42:27,321 --> 00:42:29,036
and my soul is going to leave now.

488
00:42:31,056 --> 00:42:35,904
So, the reason I cried is because I wanted Allah to give me a hundred souls,

489
00:42:36,189 --> 00:42:39,575
so that I could die this death hundred times for the sake of Allah.

490
00:42:42,963 --> 00:42:45,741
I wasn’t crying because I was afraid of death,

491
00:42:45,805 --> 00:42:49,485
I was crying because I wanted to die as a shaheed(شهيد) a hundred times.

492
00:42:50,327 --> 00:42:53,494
In another narration he said, I wanted to have souls,

493
00:42:53,857 --> 00:42:57,806
as the number of hair that I have on my skin.

494
00:42:59,457 --> 00:43:03,257
So, that I could give them for the sake of Allah one after another.

495
00:43:04,582 --> 00:43:10,906
I think that’s the level of Eeman(ايمان), that we can’t think about, we can't even comprehend.

496
00:43:12,596 --> 00:43:14,990
Allah Ho Akbar(الله اكبر) and that tells you brothers and sisters

497
00:43:15,291 --> 00:43:17,146
this religion is not a religion of talk

498
00:43:17,383 --> 00:43:20,675
it's not a religion of showing off how much knowledge you have,

499
00:43:21,882 --> 00:43:25,549
this religion is about your willingness to sacrifice for Allahعَزّوجَلّ.

500
00:43:26,983 --> 00:43:33,591
Abdullah Ibn Hudhaifah As-Sahmi(عبدالله بن حدافه السهمي) proved his Eeman(ايمان), at that particular moment.

501
00:43:33,857 --> 00:43:36,757
It’s a Mawaqif(مؤاقف) that show who you are?

502
00:43:37,204 --> 00:43:39,468
Mawqaf(مؤقف) is a standing point in your life

503
00:43:41,345 --> 00:43:44,039
at moments of ease everybody could be equal

504
00:43:44,321 --> 00:43:46,129
and you don’t really know what's going on

505
00:43:46,431 --> 00:43:52,047
but when the Fitnah(فِتْنَه) hits that’s when truth comes out of the heart.

506
00:43:53,081 --> 00:43:55,660
So, when the Fitnah(فِتْنَه) hit Abdullah Bin Hudhafah(عبدالله ابن حدافه),

507
00:43:56,086 --> 00:43:58,191
the true Abdullah Bin Hudhafah(عبدالله ابن حدافه) was revealed.

508
00:44:00,164 --> 00:44:02,823
Nobody knew Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) or anybody else

509
00:44:02,850 --> 00:44:04,760
nobody knew, who Abdullah Bin Hudhafah(عبدالله ابن حدافه) was.

510
00:44:05,703 --> 00:44:08,997
They knew him as a Sahabi(صحابي) but they didn’t really know what was inside of him,

511
00:44:09,781 --> 00:44:17,943
but this Mawqif(مؤقف) this standing point revealed the reality, of what was lingering in his heart, Al-Eeman(الايمان).

512
00:44:21,383 --> 00:44:26,315
It was the willingness to sacrifice for Allahعَزّوجَلّ and to give his soul one after another.

513
00:44:26,339 --> 00:44:35,720
You know this makes Sahabah(صحابه) special and that was something the people around them couldn’t comprehend.

514
00:44:35,781 --> 00:44:40,028
I mean with for example with this, delegation of Qura’(قراء) memorizers of Qur’an,

515
00:44:40,052 --> 00:44:43,899
which Rasool Allah ﷺ sent out to Najd(نجد), that were betrayed.

516
00:44:44,557 --> 00:44:47,752
You know when one of the Sahabah(صحابه) came in to meet with the leader of the tribe.

517
00:44:48,840 --> 00:44:50,906
The leader of the tribe gave his signal,

518
00:44:51,168 --> 00:44:55,539
so a man came with a spear and stabbed the Sahabi(صحابي) from behind him,

519
00:44:56,319 --> 00:44:59,948
so the blade came out from the front.

520
00:45:01,093 --> 00:45:07,585
So, imagine this Sahabi(صحابي) he was attacked, he was caught off guard.

521
00:45:07,610 --> 00:45:10,388
He didn’t know that somebody was planning to kill him.

522
00:45:10,478 --> 00:45:16,091
It was a surprise to him and then he sees a spear sticking out of his stomach.

523
00:45:18,504 --> 00:45:19,439
What did he say?

524
00:45:20,089 --> 00:45:21,866
A big smile on his face and he said;

525
00:45:21,938 --> 00:45:23,105
فُزْتُ وَرَبِّ الْكَعْبَةْ

526
00:45:23,597 --> 00:45:26,382
I have won in the name of Allah, I won.

527
00:45:28,886 --> 00:45:31,744
One man, who was present, he said, I couldn’t forget that.

528
00:45:32,272 --> 00:45:39,221
That statement stayed in my mind how could somebody say I won when they are dying.

529
00:45:40,569 --> 00:45:45,060
And since he didn’t know anything about Islam he went asking about this

530
00:45:46,969 --> 00:45:48,153
and then he became Muslim.

531
00:45:49,508 --> 00:45:52,694
Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله), the Sahabah(صحابه) are even giving Daw'ah(دعوة) when they are dying.

532
00:45:57,714 --> 00:46:01,109
So, the king when he saw Abdullah Bin Hudhafah(عبدالله ابن حدافه) and his determination

533
00:46:03,505 --> 00:46:04,951
he was embarrassed.

534
00:46:06,464 --> 00:46:09,051
You know, he wanted to get out something of Abdullah(عبدالله)

535
00:46:09,075 --> 00:46:15,011
he can kill him but he felt that, his pride was insulted.

536
00:46:16,508 --> 00:46:19,695
So, now the issue with the king was not of killing of Abdullah Bin Hudhafah(عبدالله ابن حدافه),

537
00:46:19,719 --> 00:46:21,930
his issue was I want to get something out of this man.

538
00:46:22,445 --> 00:46:24,754
He has to give in, he has to give me something.

539
00:46:27,401 --> 00:46:28,998
So, he told Abdullah Bin Hudhafah(عبدالله ابن حدافه),

540
00:46:31,276 --> 00:46:35,844
I am going to free you if you just going to kiss my forehead.

541
00:46:36,299 --> 00:46:42,430
Look at this, just kiss my forehead and I will let you go, "Give me something."

542
00:46:43,871 --> 00:46:46,387
He is begging Abdullah Bin Hudhafah(عبدالله ابن حدافه), the Roman king,

543
00:46:46,641 --> 00:46:48,600
Give me something! Kiss me on my forehead.

544
00:46:50,564 --> 00:46:52,966
Abdullah Bin Hudhafah(عبدالله ابن حدافه) thought about it and then he said,

545
00:46:54,119 --> 00:47:02,738
only if you going to set me free and also set all the Muslim prisoners of war free.

546
00:47:05,097 --> 00:47:06,144
The King said: I agree.

547
00:47:07,385 --> 00:47:11,343
Abdullah Bin Hudhafah(عبدالله ابن حدافه) kissed him and he got all of the Muslims free.

548
00:47:13,497 --> 00:47:17,140
Abdullah Bin Hudhafah(عبدالله ابن حدافه) goes back to Madina Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) hears the story.

549
00:47:17,733 --> 00:47:22,171
he goes to the Masjid(مسجد) Abdullah Bin Hudhafah(عبدالله ابن حدافه) is there all of the Muslims are there.

550
00:47:22,334 --> 00:47:24,726
He stands up Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said;

551
00:47:25,922 --> 00:47:30,804
It is an obligation on every Muslim to kiss the forehead of Abdullah Bin Hudhafah(عبدالله ابن حدافه)

552
00:47:31,206 --> 00:47:32,440
 and I am going to be the first

553
00:47:33,221 --> 00:47:35,203
and he kisses the forehead of Abdullah Bin Hudhafah(عبدالله ابن حدافه)

554
00:47:36,277 --> 00:47:41,775
because he saved the Muslims, he saved the Muslim prisoners of war.

555
00:47:49,302 --> 00:47:57,222
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) went to meet the reinforcement that was coming from Yemen.

556
00:47:59,028 --> 00:48:02,460
Armies were coming out of Yemen Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله) to go and fight

557
00:48:02,999 --> 00:48:06,835
and they would pass through Madina on their way to Iraq and Ash-Sham(الشام).

558
00:48:07,788 --> 00:48:11,106
So, Umar(عُمَر) went to greet them and he said;

559
00:48:11,130 --> 00:48:13,096
أَفِيْكُمْ اويس ابن عامر ؟

560
00:48:14,578 --> 00:48:16,769
Is Owais Bin Aamir(أويس بن عامر) among you?

561
00:48:17,984 --> 00:48:20,216
So, they were directing him, and Umar(عُمَر) was asking

562
00:48:20,241 --> 00:48:23,318
and he was getting closer until he reached to this man.

563
00:48:23,343 --> 00:48:26,254
And he told him; Are you Owais Bin Aamir(أويس بن عامر)? He said; "Yes I am."

564
00:48:29,278 --> 00:48:31,660
مِنْ مُرَادْ ثُمَّ مِنْ قَرْن؟

565
00:48:31,684 --> 00:48:33,495
Are you from Muraad(مراد) and then, from Qarn(قرن)?

566
00:48:33,519 --> 00:48:36,729
So, the clan is Muraad(مراد), and the tribe is Qarn(قرن). He said; Yes!

567
00:48:37,834 --> 00:48:45,747
Umar(عُمَر) said; Were you suffering from Leprosy,

568
00:48:47,126 --> 00:48:51,146
and then Allah healed you except for a size of a coin?

569
00:48:51,676 --> 00:48:52,710
He said; Yes!

570
00:48:53,992 --> 00:48:55,492
he said: Do you have a mother?

571
00:48:56,076 --> 00:48:58,409
Is your mother alive? He said; Yes!

572
00:48:59,644 --> 00:49:02,858
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said; I heard Rasool Allah ﷺ say;

573
00:49:04,464 --> 00:49:11,040
يَأْتِيْكُمْ اَويس بن عامر فِيْ اَمْدَادِ الْيَمَنْ، مِنْ مُرَادْ ثُمَّ مِنْ قَرْنََ

574
00:49:11,990 --> 00:49:16,505
Owais Bin Aamir(أويس بن عامر) is gonna come to you with reinforcements coming from Yemen

575
00:49:17,524 --> 00:49:22,411
and he is from Muraad(مراد) and then from Qarn(قرن), and he used to suffer from Leprosy,

576
00:49:22,742 --> 00:49:25,447
and then Allah healed him except the size of a coin.

577
00:49:26,219 --> 00:49:29,851
And he is very kind towards his mother,

578
00:49:31,174 --> 00:49:36,858
if you ever meet him, ask him to make Dua(دُعَا) that Allah forgives you.

579
00:49:39,137 --> 00:49:44,132
فَاِذَا فَاِنِ اسْتَطَعَّتْ فَسْئَلْه’ اَنْ يَسْتَغْفِرَهْ لَكْ

580
00:49:47,059 --> 00:49:48,770
This is a man, who is not a Sahabi(صحابي).

581
00:49:50,957 --> 00:49:53,343
Even though, he lived in the times of Rasool Allah ﷺ

582
00:49:53,550 --> 00:49:57,579
but he could not meet Rasool Allah ﷺ because he had to stay with his mother.

583
00:49:59,742 --> 00:50:02,742
And to be a Sahabi(صحابي) you have to see Rasool Allah ﷺ,

584
00:50:02,790 --> 00:50:05,980
you just can’t be a contemporary of Rasool Ullah, you have to see Rasool Ullah.

585
00:50:06,273 --> 00:50:09,816
So, he lost, the opportunity of being a Sahabi(صحابي), why?

586
00:50:10,409 --> 00:50:12,594
Because of his mother, he wanted to stay with his mother.

587
00:50:13,284 --> 00:50:16,097
He lost the opportunity of Fighting Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله)

588
00:50:16,307 --> 00:50:18,086
because he stayed behind with his mother.

589
00:50:18,456 --> 00:50:24,798
And this is the Hukum(حكم) only with fighting that is offensive not the defensive one obviously.

590
00:50:28,169 --> 00:50:36,618
So, it is quite strange to hear a statement Rasool Allah ﷺ asking the Sahabah(صحابه)

591
00:50:37,171 --> 00:50:40,792
to ask somebody, who's not a Sahabi(صحابي) to make Dua(دُعَا) for them,

592
00:50:41,249 --> 00:50:42,510
to ask Allah to forgive them.

593
00:50:46,785 --> 00:50:48,921
But this narration is in Sahih Muslim(صحيح مسلم).

594
00:50:53,110 --> 00:50:56,528
So, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب), the Khalifah(خليفه), the Ameer-Ul-Mo'mineen(امير المؤمنين)

595
00:50:57,399 --> 00:50:59,400
is telling Owais Bin Aamir(أويس بن عامر),

596
00:50:59,518 --> 00:51:00,718
اَسْتَغْفِرْلِي

597
00:51:00,977 --> 00:51:02,861
Ask Allah to forgive me.

598
00:51:03,262 --> 00:51:04,193
Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله).

599
00:51:04,953 --> 00:51:08,403
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) is asking Owais Bin Aamir(أويس بن عامر)

600
00:51:10,032 --> 00:51:12,020
to make Dua(دُعَا) for him that Allah forgives him.

601
00:51:12,893 --> 00:51:16,525
Owais Bin Aamir(أويس بن عامر) is one of the Awliya(اولياء) of Allahعَزّوجَلّ.

602
00:51:20,581 --> 00:51:25,633
Owais Bin Aamir(أويس بن عامر) makes Istighfaar(اِسْتَغْفَار) for Umar Ibn Al-Khattab رضي الله عنه

603
00:51:26,926 --> 00:51:28,032
and Umar(عُمَر) is the Khalifah(خليفه).

604
00:51:30,466 --> 00:51:34,605
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) said: "So where do you want to go?"

605
00:51:35,757 --> 00:51:37,479
Owais(اويس) said: "I want to go to Al-Koofa(الكوفه).

606
00:51:38,468 --> 00:51:44,401
Umar(عُمَر) said: "Let me write a letter, to the Governor of Kufa(كوفه) to take good care of you."

607
00:51:45,348 --> 00:51:48,976
The Khalifah(خليفه), he loves Owais(اويس), he wants to take good care of him.

608
00:51:50,074 --> 00:51:56,722
Owais(اويس) said: "Please don’t! Because I want to live in obscurity, among the layman."

609
00:51:57,780 --> 00:52:00,947
I don’t want to be known, I don’t want any special treatment.

610
00:52:01,506 --> 00:52:04,139
I want to be a unknown person Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله)

611
00:52:04,803 --> 00:52:08,598
and to live with the layman, with the common people.

612
00:52:10,242 --> 00:52:13,903
This is an example of somebody who is Abd(عبد), Taqi(تقي), Khafi(خفي).

613
00:52:14,571 --> 00:52:18,362
Somebody, who has Taqwa(تقوى) and is hidden, nobody knows him.

614
00:52:19,171 --> 00:52:20,004
Rasool Allah ﷺ says;

615
00:52:20,079 --> 00:52:21,890
اِنَّ اللهَ يُحِبَّ الْعَبْدِ تَّقِيْ اَلْخَفِيْ

616
00:52:21,915 --> 00:52:25,627
Allahعَزّوجَلّ knows the one, who is not known but has Taqwa(تقوى).

617
00:52:29,615 --> 00:52:35,707
So, he goes to Al-Kufa(الكوفه) and he settles there and nobody knows about him for a year.

618
00:52:39,305 --> 00:52:45,125
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) meets with one of the noble men of the tribe of Owais Al-Qarni(اويس القرني),

619
00:52:45,165 --> 00:52:46,982
 who are with him in Iraq in Kufa(كوفه).

620
00:52:47,734 --> 00:52:49,951
He meets him in Madina, the following year.

621
00:52:51,773 --> 00:52:54,055
So, Umar(عُمَر) is asking him about Owais Al-Qarni(اويس القرني)

622
00:52:54,804 --> 00:52:57,459
and nobody knows the special status of Owais(اويس).

623
00:52:58,742 --> 00:53:01,548
So, Umar(عُمَر), the Khalifah(خليفه) is now asking about Owais Al-Qarni(اويس القرني)

624
00:53:01,657 --> 00:53:02,400
how is he doing?

625
00:53:03,786 --> 00:53:04,926
So, this man said:

626
00:53:05,470 --> 00:53:09,104
تَرَكْتُه’ رَفْثِ الْبَيْت، قَلِيْلَ الْاَثَاثْ

627
00:53:10,572 --> 00:53:15,731
I left him in a state of poverty and his house is without furniture,

628
00:53:16,863 --> 00:53:19,481
why are you asking about this man, he is a poor man

629
00:53:19,823 --> 00:53:24,093
and he has no furniture in his house Allah O Akbar(الله اكبر), he wants to live in obscurity.

630
00:53:25,021 --> 00:53:27,396
If he had that letter from Ameer-Ul-Mo'mineen(امير المؤمنين)

631
00:53:27,421 --> 00:53:29,786
 he would be living a very comfortable life in Halal(حلال).

632
00:53:30,575 --> 00:53:35,269
But he was happy with, what Allahعَزّوجَلّ has destined for him, he was happy.

633
00:53:35,555 --> 00:53:39,067
He was happy with what Allah gave him, content.

634
00:53:41,853 --> 00:53:45,950
So, now Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) tells the man if you meet him

635
00:53:47,275 --> 00:53:51,872
tell him to make a Dua(دُعَا) for you because this is what Rasool Allah ﷺ said about him.

636
00:53:53,465 --> 00:53:55,972
So, the man go back to Owais(اويس) and he said;

637
00:53:55,997 --> 00:53:57,419
اويس اِسْتَغْفِرْلِيْ

638
00:53:57,754 --> 00:53:59,220
Ask Allah to forgive me.

639
00:54:00,816 --> 00:54:03,191
Owais(اويس) said: You ask Allah for forgiveness,

640
00:54:03,216 --> 00:54:06,461
you just came back from travelling and the Dua(دُعَا) of the traveler is accepted.

641
00:54:07,116 --> 00:54:10,118
He said; No! No! No! I want you to make Istaghfaar(استغفار) for me.

642
00:54:12,662 --> 00:54:16,171
Owais(اويس) thought about and then he said: Did you meet Umar(عُمَر)?

643
00:54:17,919 --> 00:54:18,966
He said; Yes I did.

644
00:54:20,752 --> 00:54:25,786
Owais(اويس) made Istaghfaar(استغفار) for him and the news spread.

645
00:54:29,578 --> 00:54:33,187
Suddenly, they tried, looking for Owais Al-Qarni(اويس القرني) he was nowhere to be found.

646
00:54:34,441 --> 00:54:39,427
He disappeared in order to go and live in obscurity somewhere else.

647
00:54:41,082 --> 00:54:45,033
Allah Ho Akbar(الله اكبر) running away from fame, from recognition.

648
00:54:46,849 --> 00:54:48,650
He didn’t want people to know his Taqwa(تقوي),

649
00:54:48,674 --> 00:54:50,438
he didn’t want people to know his status,

650
00:54:51,748 --> 00:54:58,881
he just disappeared to live for the sake of Allahعَزّوجَلّ, to fight in Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله)

651
00:54:59,471 --> 00:55:03,678
and to do it for Allah and Allahعَزّوجَلّ to recognize what I have done.

652
00:55:04,424 --> 00:55:05,964
I don’t want recognition from anyone.

653
00:55:07,960 --> 00:55:12,561
We ask Allahعَزّوجَلّ to give us Ikhlaas(اخلاص) in everything that we do and in everything that we say.

654
00:55:17,010 --> 00:55:21,971
Another group of Mujahideen(مجاهدين) from Yemen

655
00:55:22,690 --> 00:55:27,163
on their way back from Ash-Sham(الشام) to Yemen, they passed through Madina.

656
00:55:29,158 --> 00:55:34,582
And Umar Ibn Al-Khattab رضي الله عنه after the early prayer,

657
00:55:35,557 --> 00:55:45,148
he would bring out plates of food for the public to eat, for the travelers, for the needy.

658
00:55:46,699 --> 00:55:50,498
This was a public service that Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) was offering

659
00:55:52,319 --> 00:55:58,499
and he would do that and just present the food and, he would serve it to the people

660
00:56:00,312 --> 00:56:09,390
and stand over them to make sure that they are being served well, the Khalifah(خليفه) himself.

661
00:56:13,524 --> 00:56:21,896
So, he sees this man from this group and they are travelling back to Yemen,

662
00:56:21,920 --> 00:56:26,568
so they are in Madina, travelers, so he comes and he eats.

663
00:56:30,483 --> 00:56:33,691
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) told him: Eat with your right hand.

664
00:56:35,875 --> 00:56:39,013
He was eating with his left hand, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) is doing;

665
00:56:39,037 --> 00:56:40,515
اَمَرْ بِالْمَعْرُوْفَ، وَنَهِي الْمُنْكَرْ

666
00:56:40,540 --> 00:56:43,788
And serving, you know so many good deeds at once.

667
00:56:44,187 --> 00:56:49,057
Eat with your right hand, the man ignored Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب).

668
00:56:50,724 --> 00:56:53,369
Umar(عُمَر) told him: Eat with your right hand.

669
00:56:55,709 --> 00:56:58,666
The man said: "O Ameer-Ul-Mo'mineen(امير المؤمنين) my right hand is busy".

670
00:57:01,448 --> 00:57:05,116
So, Umar(عُمَر) left him and when he finished his meal

671
00:57:05,433 --> 00:57:08,655
Umar(عُمَر) went to the man and said: "What do you mean your right hand is busy?"

672
00:57:11,143 --> 00:57:17,585
So, the man pulls out his right arm and there was no right hand.

673
00:57:20,450 --> 00:57:22,867
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said: "مَا هَذَا؟" "What is this?"

674
00:57:24,410 --> 00:57:29,297
The man said: "I lost my right hand, when I was fighting in the Battle of Yarmook(يرموك)."

675
00:57:32,427 --> 00:57:34,977
Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله), the man didn’t want to show off,

676
00:57:35,911 --> 00:57:39,173
in front of people that he has lost his arm in Jihad(جهاد).

677
00:57:40,927 --> 00:57:42,944
And he only did it, when the Khalifah(خليفه) insisted.

678
00:57:44,515 --> 00:57:46,414
The Khalifah(خليفه) asked him first time, he ignored,

679
00:57:47,054 --> 00:57:48,983
second time, he said my right hand is busy,

680
00:57:49,867 --> 00:57:53,732
third time he just pulls out his arm and shows it to the Khalifah(خليفه).

681
00:57:56,135 --> 00:57:57,963
Look at the Ikhlaas(اخلاص) this man had.

682
00:57:58,748 --> 00:58:00,756
But then look at the question of Umar(عُمَر).

683
00:58:03,041 --> 00:58:04,500
What would you expect Umar(عُمَر) to ask?

684
00:58:05,895 --> 00:58:08,656
You know! It shows you what was on the mind of the Sahabah(صحابه).

685
00:58:11,872 --> 00:58:13,469
He said: "So, do you make a Wudhu(وضؤ)?"

686
00:58:16,298 --> 00:58:21,540
Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله), Ya'ani(يعني) you know, that’s the first thing that is triggered in the mind of Umar(عُمَر).

687
00:58:21,643 --> 00:58:22,517
 How you make Wudhu(وضؤ)?

688
00:58:23,517 --> 00:58:24,886
How do you prepare for the Salah(صلاة)?

689
00:58:26,789 --> 00:58:30,392
When Rasool Allah ﷺ was talking to the Sahabah(صحابه) about Ad-Dajjal(الدجال)

690
00:58:31,615 --> 00:58:35,663
and he said: That one day is equal to a year and next day is equal to a month,

691
00:58:36,037 --> 00:58:40,134
the third day is equal to a week and then the other days are like your regular days.

692
00:58:40,672 --> 00:58:41,949
What did the Sahabah(صحابه) say?

693
00:58:42,242 --> 00:58:44,939
O Rasool Allah ﷺ how come it's equal to a year?

694
00:58:45,102 --> 00:58:47,816
Is it because of the rotation of the globe, did it stopped?

695
00:58:48,094 --> 00:58:52,164
Can you give us a scientific explanation for that, how will the weather be?

696
00:58:52,531 --> 00:58:53,483
What did the Sahabah(صحابه) say?

697
00:58:55,862 --> 00:58:59,857
What was their concern? Look at the question, that the Sahabah(صحابه) asked. They said;

698
00:58:59,912 --> 00:59:05,039
يا رسول الله ذَالِكَ الْيَوْمَ الَّذِيْ كَسَنَعَتَكْ فِيْنَا فِيْه الصَلوةَ اليَوْمَ؟

699
00:59:05,997 --> 00:59:08,663
O Rasool Ullah that day which is as long as a year,

700
00:59:11,044 --> 00:59:15,436
is it enough to pray the five daily prayers as if it is a one day?

701
00:59:16,312 --> 00:59:18,606
So, the first thing that came to their minds was Salah(صلاة).

702
00:59:18,630 --> 00:59:22,143
How will we pray when that day is a yearlong?

703
00:59:23,507 --> 00:59:25,546
So, Umar(عُمَر) now when he saw his right hand missing

704
00:59:25,601 --> 00:59:26,914
he said, how do you make your Wudhu(وضؤ)?

705
00:59:28,461 --> 00:59:30,677
And it also shows you the care that Umar(عُمَر) had.

706
00:59:31,924 --> 00:59:37,025
The man said: I make Wudhu(وضؤ) with my left hand.

707
00:59:38,908 --> 00:59:40,279
وَالله! هُوَ الْمُعِيْنْ

708
00:59:40,986 --> 00:59:43,064
And Allah is the One, Who gives help.

709
00:59:46,480 --> 00:59:51,005
He said: "So where are you going to?" He said: "I am going back to Yemen!

710
00:59:51,613 --> 00:59:57,612
to visit my mother because I haven’t seen her for few years.

711
00:59:58,740 --> 01:00:02,564
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said: "And you are also so kind towards your mother."

712
01:00:03,201 --> 01:00:04,034
Come with me.!

713
01:00:04,955 --> 01:00:10,426
And he gives him a servant and he gives him five camels

714
01:00:12,102 --> 01:00:15,264
and he tells him, you now, welcome to leave.

715
01:00:19,268 --> 01:00:22,112
This is the care that Umar Ibn Al-Khattab رضي الله عنه had,

716
01:00:22,158 --> 01:00:25,573
for the ones, who sacrificed for the sake of Allahعَزّوجَلّ.

717
01:00:34,958 --> 01:00:40,513
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) knew what was most worthy and most valuable.

718
01:00:42,555 --> 01:00:44,789
And he wanted to give the Sahabah(صحابه) a lesson.

719
01:00:46,533 --> 01:00:48,000
So, they were sitting in a room

720
01:00:49,934 --> 01:00:53,305
and he said, Taman'nao(تَمَنَّوْا), Make a wish?

721
01:00:55,981 --> 01:01:00,007
One of the Sahabah(صحابه) said: "I wish that this room would be filled with gold,

722
01:01:01,235 --> 01:01:03,177
so that I can spend it in the path of Allah".

723
01:01:05,602 --> 01:01:07,181
He said: Taman'nao(تَمَنَّوْا), Make a wish?

724
01:01:07,923 --> 01:01:14,038
Another Sahabi(صحابي) he said: "I wish this room would be filled with jewels and gems,

725
01:01:15,245 --> 01:01:17,425
so that I can spend it in the path of Allah".

726
01:01:17,886 --> 01:01:19,060
He said: "Make a wish?"

727
01:01:19,402 --> 01:01:21,663
They said: "O Ameer-Ul-Mo'mineen(امير المؤمنين) we don’t know what to say?"

728
01:01:22,877 --> 01:01:24,165
Filled this room with what?

729
01:01:26,154 --> 01:01:35,203
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said: "My wish is that Allahعَزّوجَلّ fills this room

730
01:01:36,397 --> 01:01:40,761
with the likes of Abu Obaidah Amr Ibn Jarrah(ابو عبيدة عمرو بن جراح),

731
01:01:41,569 --> 01:01:43,518
so that I can send them Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله)".

732
01:01:45,280 --> 01:01:48,716
I wish this room is full of men like Abu Obaidah(ابوعبيدة)

733
01:01:49,564 --> 01:01:52,193
and in another narration Abu Obaidah(ابوعبيدة) and Mua’dh Ibn Jabal(معاذ ابن جبل),

734
01:01:53,392 --> 01:01:55,302
so that I can send them in path of Allah.

735
01:01:56,025 --> 01:01:57,832
Umar(عُمَر) is telling us, and telling them

736
01:01:58,771 --> 01:02:04,539
that your human resources are more important than your financial resources.

737
01:02:05,381 --> 01:02:08,042
They are more important than your bricks and mortar.

738
01:02:09,108 --> 01:02:11,412
They are more important than everything that you have.

739
01:02:11,920 --> 01:02:14,248
It is your human resources that count.

740
01:02:15,030 --> 01:02:19,253
Rasool Allah ﷺ when he passed away, he didn’t leave behind any glamorous buildings.

741
01:02:19,819 --> 01:02:25,760
The Masjid(مسجد) of Madina was mud, and the floor was sand,

742
01:02:26,446 --> 01:02:33,534
and the roof was palm leaves, and it would drip water on them when it rained.

743
01:02:35,458 --> 01:02:37,696
Rasool Allah ﷺ did not paved any roads.

744
01:02:38,513 --> 01:02:47,381
He didn’t established a financial network of business, he didn’t leave behind books.

745
01:02:48,287 --> 01:02:51,803
All what Rasool Allah ﷺ left behind was Qur’an

746
01:02:52,789 --> 01:02:57,086
and he left it behind not in Mus'haf(مصحف), not in books

747
01:02:57,746 --> 01:03:02,096
but he left it behind ingrained in the hearts of Sahabah رضي الله عنهم .

748
01:03:03,809 --> 01:03:06,300
That was the product that Rasool Allah ﷺ left behind.

749
01:03:06,569 --> 01:03:12,607
That was the effort of the Daw'ah(دعوة) of Rasool Allah ﷺ, he left behind the Sahabah(صحابه).

750
01:03:13,764 --> 01:03:17,378
And every blessing that we enjoy today is a result of that.

751
01:03:21,211 --> 01:03:25,394
The religion didn’t spread that much in the times of Rasool Allah ﷺ

752
01:03:25,829 --> 01:03:27,906
it spread in the times of Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) and Umar(عُمَر).

753
01:03:28,675 --> 01:03:31,659
It spread in the Khalifah(خليفه) of Bannu Umayyah(بَنُو اُمَيَّه) and Bannu Abbas(بنو عباس).

754
01:03:34,058 --> 01:03:37,999
In the times of Rasool Allah ﷺ Islam was limited to the Arabian Peninsula.

755
01:03:44,693 --> 01:03:49,310
Rasool Allah ﷺ, the Sahabah(صحابه) that he trained in the Madina

756
01:03:49,662 --> 01:03:53,047
or in Makkah were not many a Hundred or Hundred plus.

757
01:03:55,726 --> 01:03:59,313
The ones, who gave Bay’ah(بيعة) to him, in Bay’ah-Tur-Ridhwan(بيعة الرضوان) Fourteen Hundred (1’400).

758
01:04:00,571 --> 01:04:04,258
The ones who made a Hajj(حَجْ) Wada’a(وداع) with him, were Ninety Thousand(90,000).

759
01:04:08,394 --> 01:04:11,299
So, these are the ones, who are close to the Rasool Allah ﷺ but then

760
01:04:11,894 --> 01:04:15,770
the last year of the life of Rasool Allah ﷺ the tribes were becoming Muslim

761
01:04:15,794 --> 01:04:18,906
 but they didn’t really study much under Rasool Allah ﷺ.

762
01:04:19,607 --> 01:04:22,251
So, the Hundred and Twenty Four Thousand (124’000)

763
01:04:22,857 --> 01:04:27,214
that prayed Janazah(جنازه) on Rasool Allah ﷺ not all of them very close to him.

764
01:04:28,377 --> 01:04:30,551
Really the core group was about a Hundred.

765
01:04:31,322 --> 01:04:34,255
These were the ones, who started off with him in Makkah.

766
01:04:35,543 --> 01:04:37,258
But every one of these men

767
01:04:37,848 --> 01:04:41,996
you could just throw them anywhere in this world and just leave them, leave them alone,

768
01:04:42,472 --> 01:04:43,891
they would take care of their religion.

769
01:04:45,747 --> 01:04:49,710
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) is saying, I want such men like Abu Obaidah(ابو عبيدة)

770
01:04:49,735 --> 01:04:53,774
and Mua’dh Ibn Jabal(معاذ ابن جبل), so that I can send them out Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله).

771
01:04:55,571 --> 01:04:57,543
So, the Tarbiyya(تربيعة) is the most important thing,

772
01:04:57,694 --> 01:05:03,550
it's more important than your buildings, your institutions,

773
01:05:03,575 --> 01:05:09,657
the most important thing is the Tarbiyya(تربيعة) and that is how Islam will carry on.

774
01:05:11,093 --> 01:05:13,260
In Al-Andalus(الاندلس) they had the greatest buildings.

775
01:05:14,296 --> 01:05:16,831
They had the greatest Mosques, fabulous,

776
01:05:17,384 --> 01:05:21,564
Jami’a-Al-Qurtabah(جامع قرطبه) was the largest Masjid(مسجد) in the Muslim World until recently.

777
01:05:22,852 --> 01:05:26,140
Until the final expansion of Masjid-An-Nabawi(مسجدالنبوي),

778
01:05:26,361 --> 01:05:30,578
the Jami’a-Al-Qurtabah(جامع قرطبه) was the largest Masjid(مسجد) in the Islamic World.

779
01:05:33,332 --> 01:05:36,828
But the Muslims left it, they have left it behind why?

780
01:05:37,184 --> 01:05:38,877
Because their hearts were weak.

781
01:05:40,053 --> 01:05:43,891
They had strong buildings, the buildings stayed behind

782
01:05:44,241 --> 01:05:50,798
Spain is making a lot of money out of those buildings today, but the hearts were weak.

783
01:05:52,008 --> 01:05:55,980
The Muslims lost it on the moral front.

784
01:05:57,586 --> 01:06:02,143
Al-Ikhlaaq(الاخلاق), in the Eeman(ايمان) front before they lost it in the battle field.

785
01:06:07,893 --> 01:06:12,065
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) again, he used to give the appropriate status to people.

786
01:06:13,835 --> 01:06:18,559
Abu Sufiyan(ابوسفيان), Suhail-Ibn-Amr(سهيل ابن عمرو) two leaders of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ)

787
01:06:20,561 --> 01:06:24,625
and Sohaib(صهيب) and Bilal(بلال) two former slaves from the Quraish(قُرَيْشْ).

788
01:06:24,988 --> 01:06:28,031
Sohaib(صهيب) the Roman and Bilal(بلال) the Abyssinian, the African,

789
01:06:29,355 --> 01:06:32,907
were standing outside the office of Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب)

790
01:06:34,514 --> 01:06:35,916
seeking permission to get in.

791
01:06:36,678 --> 01:06:41,482
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) allows Sohaib(صهيب) and Bilal(بلال) the slaves to come in

792
01:06:42,358 --> 01:06:47,686
Abu Sufiyan(ابوسفيان) and Suhail(سهيل) to wait outside until he finishes with Bilal(بلال) and Sohaib(صهيب) first.

793
01:06:48,800 --> 01:06:51,725
Abu Sufiyan(ابوسفيان) complained, he said: "I have never seen a day like this.

794
01:06:52,104 --> 01:06:54,361
He allows these slaves to go in before us?"

795
01:06:56,935 --> 01:06:58,966
Suhail(سهيل) said: "I can see your anger

796
01:07:00,021 --> 01:07:05,873
but you should be angry with no one but your own self, their own selves.

797
01:07:07,505 --> 01:07:15,873
Rasool Allah ﷺ invited you and invited them and they came fast but you were slow.

798
01:07:18,303 --> 01:07:20,221
And what will you do on the day of judgment?

799
01:07:20,245 --> 01:07:22,950
When they will be invited before you and you will be waiting."

800
01:07:25,141 --> 01:07:28,195
This is not really a big deal now, we are standing outside the office of a Khalifah(خليفه),

801
01:07:28,219 --> 01:07:29,897
what will happen on the day of Judgment,

802
01:07:30,570 --> 01:07:33,434
when these men would be invited to Jannah(جنة) before you?

803
01:07:35,382 --> 01:07:40,508
You ought to cry because of your joining the caravan too late.

804
01:07:43,541 --> 01:07:46,814
And that holds true all the time,

805
01:07:48,026 --> 01:07:49,960
that holds true all the time.

806
01:07:50,490 --> 01:07:54,010
If you are joining in too late you are missing a lot, you are missing a lot.

807
01:07:55,403 --> 01:07:59,383
So, don’t miss the train. Don’t let the caravan leave without you.

808
01:08:06,327 --> 01:08:14,692
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) was in the court

809
01:08:14,717 --> 01:08:18,771
and Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) and another man came to him, they had a dispute.

810
01:08:19,697 --> 01:08:22,349
So, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) had Ali(علي) and that other man sit down.

811
01:08:23,650 --> 01:08:28,956
And then he said, to Ali(علي), "Ya Abal-Hassan(يا اباالحسن)"  O father of Al-Hassan(الحسن),

812
01:08:29,607 --> 01:08:34,431
go ahead with your side of the story and Kuniya(كنية) is a way of respect.

813
01:08:35,725 --> 01:08:38,895
He said: Abal-Hassan(اباالحسن), he is giving him his Kuniya(كنية).

814
01:08:41,500 --> 01:08:43,867
And then he asked the other man for his opinion.

815
01:08:46,221 --> 01:08:48,154
The face of Ali(علي) changed.

816
01:08:49,800 --> 01:08:52,246
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said: It seems that you are upset

817
01:08:52,800 --> 01:08:55,092
because I have equaled you to this man?

818
01:08:55,776 --> 01:08:59,553
And Wallahu ‘Alam(ولله اعلم) as I have heard but it's not in the references that I have looked up

819
01:09:00,102 --> 01:09:01,326
that this other man was a Jew.

820
01:09:02,424 --> 01:09:05,624
He said: "O Ali(علي), it seems that you are upset.

821
01:09:06,039 --> 01:09:10,336
Because I am putting you on the same footing as this man.

822
01:09:10,898 --> 01:09:16,537
Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) relative of Rasool Allah ﷺ, the husband of Fatima(فاطمه),

823
01:09:16,721 --> 01:09:18,572
the father of Al-Hassan wal Hussain(الحسن ولحسين).

824
01:09:20,096 --> 01:09:23,978
Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) said: "No that’s not why I am upset.

825
01:09:24,944 --> 01:09:27,581
I am upset because you called me with my Kuniya(كنية)

826
01:09:27,999 --> 01:09:30,284
and you didn’t call him by his Kuniya(كنية)."

827
01:09:32,327 --> 01:09:35,817
I am upset because you actually preferred me over him.

828
01:09:37,954 --> 01:09:39,259
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said;

829
01:09:41,306 --> 01:09:45,866
لَا اَبَقَانِيَ  اللهُ بِاَرْضٍ لَيْسَ فِيْهَا اَبَا الْحَسَنْ

830
01:09:47,279 --> 01:09:53,275
I ask Allah, never to allow me to live in a land, if Abal-Hassan(اباالحسن) is not around.

831
01:09:54,959 --> 01:09:59,813
I ask Allah not to allow me to live in a land, if Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) is not next to me.

832
01:10:01,284 --> 01:10:05,552
He was grateful to Ali(علي) that he had this sense of justice,

833
01:10:05,807 --> 01:10:11,378
he doesn’t even want to be given that preference.

834
01:10:11,403 --> 01:10:14,704
It's not really preference, it doesn’t affect the ruling at all

835
01:10:15,200 --> 01:10:20,200
but he doesn’t want to be spoken to in a different tone then this other man.

836
01:10:24,423 --> 01:10:29,239
We are talking about justice that to us is just an imaginary world

837
01:10:30,519 --> 01:10:32,238
because we don’t have anything to relate to now.

838
01:10:33,847 --> 01:10:36,650
We are living in systems that are so far away from ‘Adl(عدل)

839
01:10:37,410 --> 01:10:41,572
that we find it hard to grasp, what we're talking about.

840
01:10:45,459 --> 01:10:47,512
THE NEXT SECTION

841
01:10:47,537 --> 01:10:55,636
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) again had this reverence, dignity, presence,

842
01:10:56,281 --> 01:10:58,806
his presence was felt by everybody around him.

843
01:11:00,719 --> 01:11:07,381
Ibn Abbas(ابن عباس) says, that the barber of Umar(عُمَر) was cutting his hair

844
01:11:08,361 --> 01:11:12,986
and Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) coughed, so the man did it on himself.

845
01:11:14,104 --> 01:11:17,180
He was so afraid, because of the coughing of Umar(عُمَر).

846
01:11:18,021 --> 01:11:21,695
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب), when he knew that he gave him Forty Dinar.

847
01:11:22,716 --> 01:11:25,466
People used to have fear from Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب).

848
01:11:25,786 --> 01:11:28,330
Since, he was young he used to beat the kids with his stick

849
01:11:31,545 --> 01:11:33,874
and we talked about this woman who had a miscarriage.

850
01:11:34,866 --> 01:11:37,986
There are two version of that narration, I already mentioned to you one right?

851
01:11:38,584 --> 01:11:40,536
Did I mentioned about the woman, who had a miscarriage?

852
01:11:41,376 --> 01:11:42,786
The other version of this is that,

853
01:11:43,688 --> 01:11:45,919
there was this woman and the men were talking about her

854
01:11:45,943 --> 01:11:47,988
Allah O Alam(الله اعلم) what that exactly meant?

855
01:11:48,313 --> 01:11:51,125
But Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) wanted to investigate the matter,

856
01:11:51,149 --> 01:11:53,228
how come men are talking about this woman.

857
01:11:53,888 --> 01:11:58,234
So, he calls her in, when they told her that Umar(عُمَر) wants to meet you,

858
01:11:58,259 --> 01:12:02,703
she said: "Woe to me! What does Umar(عُمَر) want to talk to me about?"

859
01:12:03,224 --> 01:12:06,573
She was so terrified that she is going to go and meet the Khalifah(خليفه)

860
01:12:06,597 --> 01:12:11,534
and when she was walking, she had a miscarriage and the child came out

861
01:12:12,748 --> 01:12:14,515
and he cried in the beginning and then he died.

862
01:12:16,595 --> 01:12:21,388
And he had to pay blood money because of that.

863
01:12:23,574 --> 01:12:29,242
So, Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب), Uthman Ibn Affan(عثمان ابن عفان),

864
01:12:30,004 --> 01:12:32,582
Zubair Bin Awwam(ألزبير بن عوام), Talha Bin Obaidallah(طلحه بن عبيدالله),

865
01:12:32,996 --> 01:12:37,538
Sa’ad Ibn Abi Waqas(سعدابن ابي وقاص) and Abdur Rahman Ibn Awf(عبدالرحمن ابن عوف)

866
01:12:37,764 --> 01:12:41,666
they all came together for meeting. What were they discussing?

867
01:12:43,334 --> 01:12:45,947
They said: Somebody needs to go and talk to the Khalifah(خليفه)

868
01:12:48,126 --> 01:12:49,783
and tell him that people are terrified.

869
01:12:52,438 --> 01:12:56,971
And the boldest among them, in talking with Umar(عُمَر) was Abdur Rahman Ibn Awf(عبدالرحمن ابن عوف),

870
01:12:57,790 --> 01:12:59,103
he was the boldest among the group.

871
01:12:59,802 --> 01:13:01,695
So, they sent him, they said you go and talk to him.

872
01:13:04,169 --> 01:13:06,033
Now, it wasn’t easy, Ibn Abbas(ابن عباس) said;

873
01:13:06,537 --> 01:13:10,571
I had a question to ask Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) and I waited for an entire year.

874
01:13:11,742 --> 01:13:16,276
I couldn’t have the courage to go ahead and ask him, for entire year I was waiting.

875
01:13:19,383 --> 01:13:21,648
So, Abdur Rahman Ibn Awf(عبدالرحمن ابن عوف) he went to Umar(عُمَر)

876
01:13:21,672 --> 01:13:30,069
and he told him that people are afraid of you, people fear you.

877
01:13:33,306 --> 01:13:35,662
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said: Tell me the truth Abdur Rahman(عبدالرحمن).

878
01:13:37,877 --> 01:13:41,935
Did Uthman(عثمان), Ali(علي), Sa’ad(سعد), Az-Zubair(الزبير)

879
01:13:42,299 --> 01:13:45,973
were some of them send you here to talk to me about this?

880
01:13:46,715 --> 01:13:47,972
He said: Yes they did.

881
01:13:50,496 --> 01:13:51,679
Umar(عُمَر) had a feeling.

882
01:13:52,332 --> 01:13:54,341
Then Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said: "O Abdur Rahman(عبدالرحمن)

883
01:13:56,025 --> 01:13:59,747
In the name of Allah, I try to be so soft with them

884
01:14:00,400 --> 01:14:03,419
until, I felt that Allah will punish me because of that softness

885
01:14:04,376 --> 01:14:10,530
and then I became harsh until, I was afraid that Allah would punish me for my harshness.

886
01:14:10,905 --> 01:14:12,633
O Abdur Rahman(عبدالرحمن)! Tell me what to do.

887
01:14:13,434 --> 01:14:15,990
Tell me what to do, I am doing my best"

888
01:14:16,523 --> 01:14:19,439
I am trying to be soft but then I am afraid Allah will punish me for that,

889
01:14:19,766 --> 01:14:23,310
I am trying to be harsh and straight and I am afraid that Allah will punish me for that,

890
01:14:23,648 --> 01:14:28,949
Abdur Rahman(عبدالرحمن) started crying and then he walked out and he was saying;

891
01:14:31,548 --> 01:14:35,656
"Woe to them after you! Woe to them after you! Woe to them after you!"

892
01:14:37,118 --> 01:14:39,426
Abdur Rahman Ibn Awf(عبدالرحمن ابن عوف) was crying so hard,

893
01:14:40,373 --> 01:14:43,048
he was saying who will take care of this Ummah(امة) after you leave?

894
01:14:43,670 --> 01:14:46,066
Who will have a heart like you after you leave?

895
01:14:47,014 --> 01:14:51,871
Who will be so concerned about the Ummah(امة) of Muhammadﷺ like you, after you leave?

896
01:14:54,364 --> 01:14:55,742
And he left and he was crying.

897
01:14:56,969 --> 01:14:59,446
Because he felt the sincerity of Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب),

898
01:14:59,470 --> 01:15:00,700
he felt how sincere Umar(عُمَر) was.

899
01:15:00,837 --> 01:15:04,180
Umar(عُمَر) was telling him, tell me what to do, I am trying my best.

900
01:15:08,876 --> 01:15:13,391
Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله) when Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) would see how people would fear him,

901
01:15:14,280 --> 01:15:19,479
 he would say: "O Allah, You know that I fear You more than they fear me".

902
01:15:41,686 --> 01:15:46,466
 Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) was so concerned with the welfare of his people.

903
01:15:46,526 --> 01:15:48,474
He told one of his employees:

904
01:15:48,558 --> 01:15:54,465
يَاهَنِيْ اُضْمُمْ جَنَاحَكَ عَنِ الْمُسْلِمِيْنَ وَتَّقِيْ دَعْوَةَ الْمَظْلُوْمِ  فَاِنَّهَا مُسْتَجَابَ

905
01:15:54,547 --> 01:16:02,113
O Hani(هاني)! Be soft with the Muslims and beware of the Dua(دُعَا) of a oppressed

906
01:16:02,200 --> 01:16:05,040
because Allah will accept it and he said,

907
01:16:05,231 --> 01:16:20,327
وَإِيَّايَ وَنَعَمْ اِبْن عَوْف وَاِبْنِ عَفَّان، فَاِنَّهُمَا اِنْ تَهْلَكْ مَاشِئَتَ هُمَا  يَرْجِعَانِيْ اِلَى زَرْعٍ وَ نَخْلٍ

908
01:16:20,587 --> 01:16:27,041
وَاِنَّ رَبَّ سُّرَيْمَ وَالْغُنَيْمَ اِنْ تَهْلَكْ مَاشِئَتُهُمَا يَأْتِيْنِيْ بِبَنِيْهِ فَيَقُوْلُ يا امير المؤمنين

909
01:16:27,311 --> 01:16:32,873
اَفَاتَارِكْهُمْ اَنَا لَا اَبَالَكْ، فَلْمَا وَلْكَلَا اَيْسَرا عَلَيَ مِنَّ لذَّهْبِ وَالْفِضَّةْ

910
01:16:33,701 --> 01:16:36,962
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) took over some pasture land,

911
01:16:37,982 --> 01:16:42,916
this pasture land belonged to some Arab Tribes but he took it over

912
01:16:44,218 --> 01:16:48,831
why? Because he wanted to be a common pasture land for everyone.

913
01:16:50,882 --> 01:16:58,231
And he would have the camels and horses of Jihad(جهاد) also feed from that pasture land.

914
01:16:59,681 --> 01:17:02,912
"So, he told his servant and I want you to make sure

915
01:17:03,822 --> 01:17:06,146
that the Camels of Abdur Rahman Ibn Awf(عبدالرحمن ابن عوف)

916
01:17:06,756 --> 01:17:10,799
and the Camels of Uthman Ibn Affan(عثمان ابن عفان) do not feed from that pasture land,

917
01:17:11,701 --> 01:17:13,680
because if there camels die

918
01:17:14,133 --> 01:17:19,007
they have something to fall back on, they have farms that will be enough for them

919
01:17:20,172 --> 01:17:27,294
but the poor man, who has one camel or one sheep if their cattle die,

920
01:17:28,516 --> 01:17:32,666
then they are going to come to me with their children and say woe to you?

921
01:17:32,909 --> 01:17:35,302
Who do you want me to leave these children to?

922
01:17:35,713 --> 01:17:37,404
Who will take care of these children

923
01:17:38,112 --> 01:17:43,143
and it is easier for me to provide them with grass and water

924
01:17:43,514 --> 01:17:46,635
then for me to provide them with gold and silver."

925
01:17:47,022 --> 01:17:57,101
Umar(عُمَر) is saying, is this land it is easier for me to provide them with pasture land and water, right?

926
01:17:57,486 --> 01:18:00,594
But if, you prevent them from that pasture land from their grass and water

927
01:18:00,751 --> 01:18:05,833
their cattle would die and then they would come and ask me for gold and silver to feed their children

928
01:18:06,312 --> 01:18:11,531
and it is easier for me to have their cattle graze than to have me to take care of  their children.

929
01:18:12,603 --> 01:18:14,808
And he is saying keep the camels of Abdur Rahman Ibn Awf(عبدالرحمن ابن عوف)

930
01:18:14,832 --> 01:18:17,661
and Uthman Ibn Affan(عثمان ابن عفان) away because these were the millionaires.

931
01:18:18,267 --> 01:18:24,305
They can go back to their farm lands, so don't let them use this common pasture land.

932
01:18:26,035 --> 01:18:28,788
Allahعَزّوجَلّ has blessed the wealth of Abdur Rahman Ibn Awf(عبدالرحمن ابن عوف)

933
01:18:28,813 --> 01:18:30,909
and Uthman Ibn Affan(عثمان ابن عفان), so much Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله).

934
01:18:31,842 --> 01:18:38,455
Abdur Rahman Ibn Awf(عبدالرحمن ابن عوف) he comes from Makkah to Madina broke, he has nothing

935
01:18:41,514 --> 01:18:47,461
and then he was put into brotherhood, you know the Akhuwah(اخوة)

936
01:18:47,486 --> 01:18:48,929
that was between Muhajireen(مهاجرين) and Al-Ansaar(أنْصَار),

937
01:18:49,242 --> 01:18:50,288
him and Sa'ad Bin 'Ubadah(سعد ابن عبادة).

938
01:18:50,853 --> 01:18:51,988
So, Sa'ad Bin 'Ubadah(سعد ابن عبادة) told him,

939
01:18:52,012 --> 01:18:56,883
O Abdur Rahman(عبدالرحمن)! I have two wives and I am a wealthy businessman,

940
01:18:58,393 --> 01:19:05,492
I will give you half of my wealth and you choose whichever of my two wives

941
01:19:05,516 --> 01:19:11,122
you want, I will divorce her and you can marry her, amazing sacrifice!.

942
01:19:11,926 --> 01:19:13,146
Abdur Rahman Ibn Awf(عبدالرحمن ابن عوف) said,

943
01:19:13,170 --> 01:19:15,389
بَارَكَ اللهُ لَكَ فِيْ مَالِكَ وَ اَهْلِكْ

944
01:19:15,420 --> 01:19:20,828
May Allah bless your wives and your wealth, I do not need either.

945
01:19:21,890 --> 01:19:26,046
All that I want from you is to show me market place of Madina.

946
01:19:26,722 --> 01:19:28,288
دُلَّنِيْ عَلى سُوْقِ الْمَدِيْنَةَ ؟

947
01:19:28,582 --> 01:19:30,695
Where is the market place?

948
01:19:32,354 --> 01:19:36,222
He gives him the directions and Abdur Rahman Ibn Awf(عبدالرحمن ابن عوف) starts from scratch.

949
01:19:37,747 --> 01:19:41,899
A short while later Rasool Allah ﷺ sees Abdur Rahman Ibn Awf(عبدالرحمن ابن عوف).

950
01:19:41,924 --> 01:19:47,567
In those days the women would use this yellow powder for a make-up.

951
01:19:50,932 --> 01:19:55,609
In Arabic it's called horud(هُرُدْ),

952
01:19:56,167 --> 01:19:59,077
I don't remember the translation of it in English, it's actually a spice

953
01:19:59,542 --> 01:20:05,132
but it's yellowish in color and they would use it as make-up.

954
01:20:08,249 --> 01:20:12,325
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ sees Abdur Rahman Ibn Awf(عبدالرحمن ابن عوف) with this make-up on his face,

955
01:20:14,973 --> 01:20:17,132
it's not for men, this is for a women.

956
01:20:17,707 --> 01:20:19,966
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ tells him what's this on your face?

957
01:20:21,496 --> 01:20:24,684
Abdur Rahman Ibn Awf(عبدالرحمن ابن عوف) said: I got married.

958
01:20:26,250 --> 01:20:28,808
You know, it's like a lipstick proof.

959
01:20:29,937 --> 01:20:33,212
So he had that make-up on his face, so Rasool Allah ﷺ said: What is this? He said: I got married.

960
01:20:35,175 --> 01:20:37,006
So, he said: What did you pay her as a Mahr(مهر)?

961
01:20:37,030 --> 01:20:39,569
Because he know that Abdur Rahman(عبدالرحمن) came broke, he had nothing.

962
01:20:40,831 --> 01:20:42,741
Rasool Ullah wanted to get to know how did he get married?

963
01:20:43,589 --> 01:20:47,427
He said: Yes I had paid her Mahr(مهر), this amount of gold.

964
01:20:48,333 --> 01:20:52,799
He has already made enough money that he was giving Mahr(مهر) in gold.

965
01:20:56,656 --> 01:21:01,765
So, he was a man, who could put his hand on rocks and they would turn into gold, blessed.

966
01:21:02,515 --> 01:21:04,550
Allah has blessed the Rizq(رزق) of Abdur Rahman Ibn Awf(عبدالرحمن ابن عوف)

967
01:21:04,937 --> 01:21:06,980
and so was the case with Uthman Ibn Affan(عثمان ابن عفان).

968
01:21:08,588 --> 01:21:10,756
So, Umar(عُمَر) is saying keep their camels away

969
01:21:12,354 --> 01:21:14,357
Allah has blessed their wealth don't worry about them.

970
01:21:17,276 --> 01:21:18,787
And then Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) said;

971
01:21:20,314 --> 01:21:25,830
And he is talking about this poor man, who would come with his goat and camel and he said;

972
01:21:26,259 --> 01:21:34,584
وَاَيْمُ الله؟ اِنَّهُمْ لَا يَرَوْنَ، اَنِّيْ ظَلَمْتَهُمْ اِنَّهَا لَا بِلَادُهُمْ قَاتَلُوْ عَلَيْهَا

973
01:21:35,225 --> 01:21:37,763
فِي الْجَاهِلِيَّةْ وَاَسْلَمُوْا عَلَيْهَا فِي الْاِسْلَامْ

974
01:21:38,487 --> 01:21:44,463
In the name of Allah, they think that, I have oppressed them, this was their land,

975
01:21:45,260 --> 01:21:47,585
they fought over this land in Jahiliyah(جاهليه)

976
01:21:48,277 --> 01:21:51,991
and when they became Muslim they became Muslim over this land

977
01:21:52,417 --> 01:21:56,280
and now I have took away from them and in the name of Allah,

978
01:21:56,620 --> 01:22:02,275
if it wasn't because of the money that I am getting for it

979
01:22:03,037 --> 01:22:06,791
to send out the armies to fight in the path of Allahعَزّوجَلّ,

980
01:22:07,021 --> 01:22:09,637
I wouldn't have taken an inch of their land.

981
01:22:11,063 --> 01:22:14,414
If it wasn't because I want to send out the armies Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله)

982
01:22:14,657 --> 01:22:17,751
I wouldn't have taken away that land, it belongs to them.

983
01:22:20,071 --> 01:22:24,517
And this shows you the importance that Umar(عُمَر) was placing on Jihad(جهاد) Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله).

984
01:22:26,517 --> 01:22:28,851
He was investing for that.

985
01:22:31,283 --> 01:22:36,536
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) would teach the leaders lessons,

986
01:22:37,002 --> 01:22:38,599
he would teach the leaders lesson.

987
01:22:40,587 --> 01:22:44,383
Umar(عُمَر) received a complaint from the people in Makkah

988
01:22:45,020 --> 01:22:48,481
that Abu Sufiyan(ابوسفيان) is building a house

989
01:22:49,004 --> 01:22:52,117
and he is preventing the passage of water to come to us.

990
01:22:53,083 --> 01:22:58,824
So, Umar(عُمَر) goes to him, this is in Makkah and Abu Sufiyan(ابوسفيان) is standing there

991
01:22:58,849 --> 01:23:00,588
and they are building this house for him.

992
01:23:01,194 --> 01:23:03,890
So, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) with his stick he points to this rock

993
01:23:03,915 --> 01:23:05,657
and he says, take away that rock,

994
01:23:06,474 --> 01:23:07,189
so he takes away,

995
01:23:07,332 --> 01:23:08,236
take this one away,

996
01:23:08,617 --> 01:23:09,332
take this one,

997
01:23:09,736 --> 01:23:10,338
take this one,

998
01:23:10,606 --> 01:23:11,268
take this one,

999
01:23:11,609 --> 01:23:14,242
and Abu Sufiyan(ابوسفيان) is bending down and taking it away.

1000
01:23:15,073 --> 01:23:16,538
Then Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) said;

1001
01:23:18,019 --> 01:23:24,551
اَلْحَمْدُ لله اَلَّذِيْ جَعَلَ عُمر يَأْمُرُ اَبَى سُفِيَان بِبَطْنِ مَكَّةْ فَيُطِيْعُوْا ؛

1002
01:23:27,208 --> 01:23:35,628
 Al-Hamdolillah(الحمدلله), who put Umar(عُمَر) in a position to give orders to Abu Sufiyan(ابو سفيان)

1003
01:23:36,244 --> 01:23:39,544
in Makkah and Abu Sufiyan(ابوسفيان) obeys him.

1004
01:23:41,087 --> 01:23:44,103
Abu Sufiyan(ابوسفيان) at one point of time was a leader of Makkah.

1005
01:23:44,473 --> 01:23:47,607
The indisputable leader of Makkah.

1006
01:23:50,090 --> 01:23:54,600
He was the leader of the armies, against Rasool Allah ﷺ

1007
01:23:54,625 --> 01:23:56,758
he comes from the noble family of Bannu Umayyah(بَنُواُمَيَّه).

1008
01:23:56,783 --> 01:23:58,818
And Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) was Umair(عمير),

1009
01:23:59,751 --> 01:24:02,329
he comes from the small clane of Bannu Odaey(بنو عديئ).

1010
01:24:02,547 --> 01:24:07,906
He couldn't have dreamt of becoming one day a leader.

1011
01:24:09,333 --> 01:24:13,344
And now, Umar(عُمَر) is giving instructions to Abu Sufiyan(ابوسفيان). Do this, do that.

1012
01:24:14,426 --> 01:24:19,606
He said: Al-Hamdolillah(الحمدلله), Who put me in this position to bring justice.

1013
01:24:21,400 --> 01:24:25,504
Oyainah bin Hassan(عيينه بن حصن) again, this man, this Bedouin leader.

1014
01:24:26,241 --> 01:24:27,963
He was sitting with Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب)

1015
01:24:28,122 --> 01:24:34,700
and there was a commoner, a lay man, poor man, Bedouin sitting there

1016
01:24:36,111 --> 01:24:43,997
 and he is talking so Oyainah(عيينه) makes fun of him and ridicules that man.

1017
01:24:45,437 --> 01:24:51,084
So, the man starts responding back, Oyainah(عيينه) cuts him off

1018
01:24:51,109 --> 01:24:53,839
and says: Who are you to talk to me in such manner?

1019
01:24:54,515 --> 01:24:57,057
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) interrupted Oyainah(عيينه) and said;

1020
01:24:59,937 --> 01:25:02,949
"That you need to be humble in Islam

1021
01:25:03,937 --> 01:25:09,638
and in the name of Allah I am not going to allow you out

1022
01:25:10,814 --> 01:25:14,958
until, this man makes Shafa'a(شفاع) for you.

1023
01:25:17,119 --> 01:25:21,736
You're going to have to please him and make him appeal for you,

1024
01:25:23,318 --> 01:25:24,691
so that I will be please with you.

1025
01:25:25,300 --> 01:25:28,404
Now, Oyainah(عيينه) has to beg this man for forgiveness

1026
01:25:28,574 --> 01:25:32,078
and ask him to make an appeal for him with Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب).

1027
01:25:32,910 --> 01:25:34,456
He said: You need to be humble in Islam,

1028
01:25:34,706 --> 01:25:40,853
don't have this pride, don't be arrogant you are Muslim now, throw this arrogance away.

1029
01:25:49,648 --> 01:25:54,599
SOME OF THE AMR BIL-MAROOF WA NAHI ANIL MUNKAR(امر بالمعروف ونهي عن المنكر) OF UMAR BIN KHATTAB رضي الله عنه

1030
01:25:58,423 --> 01:26:01,216
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) saw a man and woman talking,

1031
01:26:01,579 --> 01:26:07,515
it was at night talking in the public in street of Madina.

1032
01:26:08,486 --> 01:26:11,171
He came with a stick and hit the man.

1033
01:26:12,824 --> 01:26:15,327
So, the man said: What did I do wrong?

1034
01:26:15,925 --> 01:26:24,497
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) said: Why are you talking with this woman in the street?

1035
01:26:26,328 --> 01:26:28,004
The man said: This is my wife.

1036
01:26:29,586 --> 01:26:30,946
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) said;

1037
01:26:31,520 --> 01:26:35,246
You shouldn't be talking to her like that when there is nobody around

1038
01:26:35,621 --> 01:26:38,511
because this is going to make people slander you.

1039
01:26:39,895 --> 01:26:43,383
She is in Hijab(حجاب) people cannot see her, they don't know who she is.

1040
01:26:44,056 --> 01:26:45,551
So, people are going to slander you.

1041
01:26:46,181 --> 01:26:53,493
Yes she is your wife, and you have absolutely the right to talk to her, where ever you want.

1042
01:26:53,904 --> 01:26:57,230
However, is going to cause people to slander you.

1043
01:26:58,255 --> 01:27:01,916
Let me continue then we will talk about the lessons.

1044
01:27:03,216 --> 01:27:06,924
So, the man said: O Ameer-Ul-Mo'mineen(امير المؤمنين)! We just arrived to Madina,

1045
01:27:06,949 --> 01:27:09,795
these were foreigners and we were discussing, where to stay?

1046
01:27:13,221 --> 01:27:17,984
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) gave him the stick and said: Hit me, hit me back.

1047
01:27:19,864 --> 01:27:22,055
The man said: I won't, he said hit me back

1048
01:27:22,161 --> 01:27:24,724
three times and the man said: No! I forgive you.

1049
01:27:26,580 --> 01:27:27,527
Number 1.

1050
01:27:30,337 --> 01:27:36,969
We shouldn't put ourselves in positions that would give people an excuse to talk about us.

1051
01:27:39,605 --> 01:27:41,439
It is absolutely fine for him to do that.

1052
01:27:41,464 --> 01:27:47,492
Rasool Allah ﷺ he was once it was night and he was speaking to Safiyah(صفيه), his wife

1053
01:27:48,667 --> 01:27:49,849
and there was nobody around.

1054
01:27:50,233 --> 01:27:52,752
So, two Sahabah(صحابه) were passing by and Rasool Ullah stopped them

1055
01:27:53,021 --> 01:27:55,557
and He said: Come here! This is my wife Safiyah(صفيه).

1056
01:27:57,030 --> 01:27:59,692
They said; O messenger of Allah we wouldn't have any doubts in you.

1057
01:28:01,034 --> 01:28:04,874
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: I don’t want Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ) to come to you.

1058
01:28:10,026 --> 01:28:12,884
So, Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ) plays games.

1059
01:28:15,208 --> 01:28:18,321
A person could be absolutely innocent

1060
01:28:20,231 --> 01:28:27,677
but because you see them in certain posture, place, condition, you become suspicious,

1061
01:28:28,236 --> 01:28:32,925
Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ) comes to you and builds up a scenario

1062
01:28:34,434 --> 01:28:38,906
and then you go and tell it to somebody and they add some salt and pepper to it.

1063
01:28:39,981 --> 01:28:43,736
And then it goes to the next person, and they load it with spices.

1064
01:28:44,473 --> 01:28:49,308
And then it goes to the next person and suddenly the story is blown out of proportion,

1065
01:28:49,735 --> 01:28:56,252
Chinese whisper, that’s a game of Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ).

1066
01:28:56,990 --> 01:28:59,790
It is wrong for the people to slander you.

1067
01:29:02,284 --> 01:29:05,413
It is wrong! Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) was not saying that the people have the right to make a Gheebah(غيبه)

1068
01:29:05,461 --> 01:29:06,968
 but Umar(عُمَر) is saying, these are people.

1069
01:29:07,332 --> 01:29:12,365
People are people and they are going to commit these sins don't put yourself in that situation.

1070
01:29:15,961 --> 01:29:19,238
The second thing, look at the innocence and the purity of Madina,

1071
01:29:19,270 --> 01:29:23,616
Allah!!! what if Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) would see for example London underground

1072
01:29:24,519 --> 01:29:28,179
and how people behave there as if they are their private bedroom.

1073
01:29:29,036 --> 01:29:30,036
(اعوذ بالله)

1074
01:29:31,864 --> 01:29:36,836
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) saw a man talking to a woman in the street and he didn't like that.

1075
01:29:39,919 --> 01:29:44,411
 We have become desensitized.

1076
01:29:45,614 --> 01:29:48,914
You know we see the haram(حرام) and it doesn't affect us anymore.

1077
01:29:48,939 --> 01:29:50,898
Umar(عُمَر) didn't like what he saw.

1078
01:29:52,406 --> 01:29:54,747
We see all of this haram(حرام) around us.

1079
01:29:55,308 --> 01:30:05,340
Billboards, TV, newspapers, you see it on the streets, and it's going to get worse,

1080
01:30:05,365 --> 01:30:13,833
Rasool Allah ﷺ says; " A time will come when a man and woman would commit a Zinah(زناء) on the street

1081
01:30:14,389 --> 01:30:19,838
 and the best of people would be, the one to tell them, can you please move a side".

1082
01:30:20,557 --> 01:30:23,124
Not telling them to stop the Haram(حرام) but just move a side.

1083
01:30:23,964 --> 01:30:25,085
These are the times of Fittan(فتن)

1084
01:30:26,960 --> 01:30:31,230
but it is not that much different in some western countries.

1085
01:30:32,335 --> 01:30:35,769
And Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله) it's leaving a bad effect on us.

1086
01:30:36,453 --> 01:30:42,542
We ask Allahعَزّوجَلّ to pure our hearts from this Fahisha(فاحشه) and to keep us away from the Fitnah(فتنه)."

1087
01:30:45,892 --> 01:30:47,793
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) saw a man begging

1088
01:30:48,663 --> 01:30:54,921
and he had some sacks of food hanging to his shoulders.

1089
01:30:56,140 --> 01:31:00,850
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) grab the food and he gave it to the camel of Sadaqah(صدقه)

1090
01:31:01,038 --> 01:31:02,653
and said: Go and beg if you want.

1091
01:31:03,938 --> 01:31:05,978
You are begging and you already have food with you.

1092
01:31:06,944 --> 01:31:07,899
Why are you begging?

1093
01:31:08,677 --> 01:31:10,010
He takes it away from him.

1094
01:31:11,220 --> 01:31:15,474
So, next time you see the beggar take that plate with all the coins in it

1095
01:31:15,522 --> 01:31:17,245
and tell them to beg not, don't do that.

1096
01:31:18,231 --> 01:31:19,622
Becareful don’t do that.

1097
01:31:23,996 --> 01:31:29,902
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) saw a man walking lazily with pride.

1098
01:31:31,027 --> 01:31:33,473
His hands and feet are swinging around.

1099
01:31:36,689 --> 01:31:40,138
I can may imagine like rappers would walk.

1100
01:31:42,364 --> 01:31:46,222
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب), he uses his Durrah(دُرَّة).

1101
01:31:48,499 --> 01:31:49,960
Stop walking like that.

1102
01:31:51,280 --> 01:31:53,495
The man said: I can't! He said: You can't?

1103
01:31:54,282 --> 01:31:55,516
He teaches him a second lesson,

1104
01:31:58,048 --> 01:32:01,501
so he changes the way he walks and then he came back and he said,

1105
01:32:01,830 --> 01:32:04,638
 Alhamdulillah(الحمدلله) to you Umar(عُمَر), that was a Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ) that left me.

1106
01:32:05,357 --> 01:32:07,150
He said: I changed my ways.

1107
01:32:08,545 --> 01:32:13,410
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) saw another man who was pretending to be a good Muslim.

1108
01:32:14,703 --> 01:32:16,103
Pretending to be a Abid(عابد).

1109
01:32:16,822 --> 01:32:25,758
You know some people, they could be full of energy, explosive, active, hyper active,

1110
01:32:26,804 --> 01:32:30,387
when they are not practicing, on the street, street boys,

1111
01:32:31,552 --> 01:32:37,994
and then they start practicing Islam, and somehow they get into some brands of Islam,

1112
01:32:38,529 --> 01:32:42,508
that teach them that, you need to be passive, you need to cool down.

1113
01:32:43,414 --> 01:32:48,180
So, they start dressing differently, and when they walk now, they walk as if they are dead.

1114
01:32:48,664 --> 01:32:50,473
Like Zombies coming out of graves,

1115
01:32:51,164 --> 01:32:54,320
and they dangle their hands, and their eyes become very dizzy,

1116
01:32:54,935 --> 01:32:57,637
and they talk softly, and when they come and give you Salam(سلام),

1117
01:32:57,662 --> 01:32:59,884
and they bend over like that and fall down

1118
01:33:01,685 --> 01:33:06,298
and they become very, very, very, soft and they think that, that is Zuhd(زهد).

1119
01:33:11,093 --> 01:33:16,249
So, a woman saw such men after the times of Umar(عُمَر), when Umar(عُمَر) has already passed away.

1120
01:33:17,877 --> 01:33:20,112
She said: Who are these? They said: These are Nastik(ناستك)

1121
01:33:20,392 --> 01:33:22,933
they were walking like this and dressed in different clothes

1122
01:33:23,493 --> 01:33:25,211
and walkingdown the streets lazily.

1123
01:33:26,743 --> 01:33:30,890
She said: These are Nustak(نستاك) these are people, who devoted themselves to worshipping Allah.

1124
01:33:32,555 --> 01:33:33,901
She said: No they are not.

1125
01:33:34,752 --> 01:33:36,996
The real Nasik(ناسك) was Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب).

1126
01:33:38,536 --> 01:33:41,233
And Umar(عُمَر) when he would walk he would walk fast,

1127
01:33:42,075 --> 01:33:44,603
and when he would talk you would definitely hear him,

1128
01:33:45,445 --> 01:33:47,606
and when he strikes, he strikes hard.

1129
01:33:50,007 --> 01:33:52,178
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) actually in his life time

1130
01:33:52,546 --> 01:33:56,048
he saw one of these men, walking down the street.

1131
01:33:57,736 --> 01:34:00,204
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب), he didn't even talk to him

1132
01:34:00,229 --> 01:34:02,922
he went straight up to him started beating him and said;

1133
01:34:03,572 --> 01:34:06,392
لَا تُمِتْ عَلَيْنَا دِيْنَنَا اَمَاتَكَ الله

1134
01:34:06,963 --> 01:34:10,182
Do not make our religion dead, may Allah give you death.

1135
01:34:11,259 --> 01:34:16,830
You are killing our religion, you are making our religion a religion of passiveness, religion of laziness.

1136
01:34:17,652 --> 01:34:18,827
 What is this way of walking?

1137
01:34:20,014 --> 01:34:21,808
You know pretending to be humble.

1138
01:34:24,210 --> 01:34:27,012
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) wanted this Ummah(امة) to be strong.

1139
01:34:28,604 --> 01:34:34,014
He wanted the Ummah(امة) to be an Ummah(امة) of fighters Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله)

1140
01:34:34,039 --> 01:34:36,651
 people who would spread the religion Fee-Sabeel-Lillah عَزّوجَلّ.

1141
01:34:37,100 --> 01:34:43,401
He didn't want to deal with people who are chicken, who are weak, who are feeble,

1142
01:34:43,449 --> 01:34:47,466
he wanted a strong Ummah(امة) and that is the teaching of Islam.

1143
01:34:48,077 --> 01:34:52,138
اَلْمُؤمِنَ الْقَوِّيْ خَيْرُا اَحَبِّ اِلَى الله مِنَ الْمُؤمِنَ الضَّعِيْفْ

1144
01:34:52,819 --> 01:34:57,096
The strong believer is better in the eyes of Allah then the weak believer.

1145
01:34:58,905 --> 01:35:01,507
So, this is a religion of strength.

1146
01:35:02,330 --> 01:35:03,949
Allahعَزّوجَلّ tells Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل);

1147
01:35:03,973 --> 01:35:05,918
خُذُوْا مَا آتَيْنَكُمْ بِقُوَّةْ

1148
01:35:06,553 --> 01:35:08,680
"Take what we have given you with strength".

1149
01:35:09,005 --> 01:35:11,112
And Allahعَزّوجَلّ tells Yahyaعليه السّلام,

1150
01:35:11,378 --> 01:35:14,126
يَا يَحْيى خُذِ الْكِتَابَ بِقُوَّةْ

1151
01:35:14,150 --> 01:35:16,464
Take what we have given you Al-Kitab(الكتاب) with strength.

1152
01:35:17,742 --> 01:35:20,866
So, this is not a religion of weakness.

1153
01:35:23,225 --> 01:35:28,140
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) would encourage exercise and he didn't like obesity.

1154
01:35:29,249 --> 01:35:31,944
He was against obesity, in fact he said,

1155
01:35:32,476 --> 01:35:35,745
اَيُّهَا النَّاسْ اِيَّاكُمْ وَالْبِطْنَهْ عَنِ الطَعَامْ

1156
01:35:36,547 --> 01:35:40,920
O people beware of over eating.

1157
01:35:41,625 --> 01:35:43,591
فَاِنَّهَا مَكْسَلَةٌ عَنَّ الصَّلوةْ

1158
01:35:43,884 --> 01:35:46,005
Because it makes you lazy in your Salah(صلاة).

1159
01:35:46,407 --> 01:35:47,526
مَفْسَدَهْ الِلْجِسْمْ

1160
01:35:47,821 --> 01:35:49,395
It makes your body weak.

1161
01:35:49,727 --> 01:35:50,919
وَمُوْرِثَ الِسَّقَمْ

1162
01:35:51,157 --> 01:35:53,432
And it makes you un healthy.

1163
01:35:55,402 --> 01:35:57,968
وَاِنَّ الله يَبْغَضُ الْحَبْرَصَ ثَمِيْنْ

1164
01:35:58,238 --> 01:36:00,554
And Allah dislikes the obese man.

1165
01:36:02,175 --> 01:36:05,036
وَلَكِنْ عَلَيْكُمْ بِالْقَصْدِ فِيْ قُوْتِكُمْ

1166
01:36:05,644 --> 01:36:08,881
And you should be modest in your food.

1167
01:36:09,816 --> 01:36:13,252
فَاِنَّه’ اَدْنَى مِنَّ الصَّلَاحِ وَ بَعْدَ عَنِ السَّرَفْ

1168
01:36:13,420 --> 01:36:16,922
Because that is closer to righteousness and further from access.

1169
01:36:17,138 --> 01:36:19,173
وَاَقْوَى عَلى عِبَادَةِ الله عزوجل

1170
01:36:19,388 --> 01:36:22,080
And it makes you stronger in worshipping Allah.

1171
01:36:22,412 --> 01:36:26,082
وَلَنْ يَهْلَكَ عَبْدٌ حَتى يُئْثِرَةْ شَهْوَاتُه’ عَلى دِيْنِه

1172
01:36:27,672 --> 01:36:40,022
And you will perish when your desires become more likable to you then Allahعَزّوجَلّ or your religion.

1173
01:36:40,307 --> 01:36:45,951
When your desires become dearer to you then your religion that is when you would perish.

1174
01:36:49,611 --> 01:36:51,048
When we talk about obesity

1175
01:36:51,088 --> 01:36:56,476
we're talking about obesity caused by over eating not by health reasons.

1176
01:36:56,515 --> 01:37:00,334
Some people genetically have that, this is not talking about that.

1177
01:37:00,808 --> 01:37:04,570
I don’t want anybody to assume that because Allah created them like that

1178
01:37:05,051 --> 01:37:06,272
Allah does not like them.

1179
01:37:07,660 --> 01:37:13,512
This is talking about obesity that is caused by over eating and that is unhealthy.

1180
01:37:15,076 --> 01:37:23,207
If you are overweight even if it is caused by genetic reasons try to lose weight.

1181
01:37:23,813 --> 01:37:25,567
Try to lose weight and exercise.

1182
01:37:28,665 --> 01:37:30,715
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) saw a man with a big belly.

1183
01:37:33,948 --> 01:37:40,139
You know they say, don't take this saying for granted,

1184
01:37:40,784 --> 01:37:44,386
they say the signs of dignity and wisdom are three.

1185
01:37:46,617 --> 01:37:53,600
The moustache, the bald head and a big belly.

1186
01:37:54,704 --> 01:37:56,387
Obviously that’s not true.!

1187
01:37:58,072 --> 01:38:02,173
It say that you need to have a belly as big as when you want to scratch it,

1188
01:38:02,232 --> 01:38:04,647
you have to extend your hand as far as you can.

1189
01:38:07,021 --> 01:38:10,488
That's a big belly.

1190
01:38:12,453 --> 01:38:18,444
In our old books in Al-Mustazraf(المستذرف) it says that,

1191
01:38:21,678 --> 01:38:24,965
they asked a Bedouin when do you know, when you are full?

1192
01:38:24,990 --> 01:38:26,518
When you do you know, when you have eaten enough?

1193
01:38:27,850 --> 01:38:32,000
He said: When I can't tell the difference between the heavens and earth,

1194
01:38:33,269 --> 01:38:35,761
and I can't tell the difference between Nafl(نفل) and Fard(فرض),

1195
01:38:36,785 --> 01:38:42,062
and I can't tell the difference between length and height that is when I had enough food.

1196
01:38:47,962 --> 01:38:53,177
حِيْنَ لَا اُفَرِّقْ بَيْنَ السَّمَآءِ وَ الْاَرْضْ، وَطُّوْلِ مِنَ الّعَرْضْ، وَالنَّفْلِ مِنَّ الْفَرْضَ

1197
01:38:56,264 --> 01:38:59,184
So, a man came to Umar(عُمَر) and he had a big belly,

1198
01:38:59,733 --> 01:39:01,396
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) told him what is this?

1199
01:39:03,045 --> 01:39:06,445
He said: This is بركة من الله، this is a blessings from Allah,

1200
01:39:07,351 --> 01:39:09,962
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) said: No! It’s a punishment from Allah.

1201
01:39:11,570 --> 01:39:13,365
This is not a blessing this a punishment

1202
01:39:13,973 --> 01:39:16,001
What are you doing dragging that thing, in front of you?

1203
01:39:20,074 --> 01:39:24,994
So, obviously this is something for the brothers, they are the ones who tend to have big bellies,

1204
01:39:25,427 --> 01:39:30,070
try to exercise brothers.

1205
01:39:30,593 --> 01:39:31,717
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) says;

1206
01:39:31,741 --> 01:39:35,145
عَلِّمُ اَوْلَادَكُمُ السِّبَاحْ وَرِمَايَا وَرَكُوْبِ الْخَيْلَ

1207
01:39:35,813 --> 01:39:37,384
Teach your children swimming

1208
01:39:37,630 --> 01:39:43,061
and Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله) swimming is the best exercise for toning your muscles,

1209
01:39:44,236 --> 01:39:52,188
swimming, target shooting and riding horses.

1210
01:39:56,158 --> 01:44:00,962
REPEAT PLZ DELETE IT

1211
01:44:00,993 --> 01:44:05,591
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) by the way he had some amazing teachings.

1212
01:44:07,150 --> 01:44:13,430
He sent a letter to the Sahabah(صحابه), up north in Azerbaijan.

1213
01:44:15,231 --> 01:44:18,203
He got a sense that may be they are getting into comfortable life.

1214
01:44:19,599 --> 01:44:25,377
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) was developing, no he wasn't developing he was carrying on,

1215
01:44:26,678 --> 01:44:30,167
 the military tradition that was started by Rasool Allah ﷺ

1216
01:44:31,109 --> 01:44:34,584
men are suppose to be soldiers and live a military life.

1217
01:44:35,346 --> 01:44:38,790
That was the life of Sahaba رضي الله عنهم it wasn't a civilian life.

1218
01:44:39,424 --> 01:44:41,993
It was a life a soldier, a life of a military.

1219
01:44:43,213 --> 01:44:50,409
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) was getting a sense that may be some of them are settling down to civilian life.

1220
01:44:51,278 --> 01:44:53,405
They were leaving the life of Murabiteen(مرابطين)

1221
01:44:54,332 --> 01:44:57,827
so, Umar(عُمَر) sends them a letter. He says,

1222
01:44:59,299 --> 01:45:00,439
 "إِخْشَوْشَنُوْا"

1223
01:45:01,805 --> 01:45:08,870
Be rough, and tough, and follow the way of your father.

1224
01:45:09,050 --> 01:45:09,790
 "وَتَمَعْدَدُوْا"

1225
01:45:10,776 --> 01:45:12,991
Follow the way of your forefathers.

1226
01:45:13,015 --> 01:45:15,527
Therefore, fathers even though they were living in the time of Jahiliyah(جاهليه)

1227
01:45:15,816 --> 01:45:18,939
but they were the men of desert, and he said:

1228
01:45:18,963 --> 01:45:22,501
Wear the clothes of your father Ismail(اِسْماعِيْل),

1229
01:45:23,092 --> 01:45:26,220
the Izaar(ازار) and stay away from the clothes of Al-'Ajam(العجم),

1230
01:45:26,779 --> 01:45:28,876
stay away from the clothes of non-Arabs.

1231
01:45:28,900 --> 01:45:33,379
The non-Arabs in those days were the people of the civilization,

1232
01:45:33,403 --> 01:45:34,946
the Roman and Persian Empire.

1233
01:45:35,399 --> 01:45:38,605
So, they have very comfortable, expensive, luxurious clothes.

1234
01:45:38,906 --> 01:45:42,358
While the Arabs were the poor people of the world they came from the desert.

1235
01:45:42,940 --> 01:45:45,957
He said: Stay away from the clothes of the non-Muslims

1236
01:45:46,267 --> 01:45:47,983
and wear that clothes of your fathers.

1237
01:45:49,018 --> 01:45:54,232
And then he said, and I want you to go with a bare top.

1238
01:45:55,551 --> 01:46:00,931
They use to have two pieces of Izaar(ازار) one to cover the top and one to cover the bottom.

1239
01:46:01,130 --> 01:46:04,933
He said: Go with the bare top. Take the one on the top off.

1240
01:46:06,296 --> 01:46:13,417
And I  want you to walk bare foot, take your shoes off and walk bare foot and

1241
01:46:14,624 --> 01:46:17,482
عَلَيْكُمْ بِالشَّمْسِ فَاِنَّ حَمَامٌ العَرَبْ

1242
01:46:18,877 --> 01:46:27,617
And stand under the sun because it is the bathing of the Arabs and he said,

1243
01:46:28,637 --> 01:46:30,402
وَسْعَوْا بَيْنَ الْاَغْرَاضْ

1244
01:46:31,016 --> 01:46:33,940
And I want you to walk fast and run between the targets.

1245
01:46:34,155 --> 01:46:38,805
In those days the target shooting practice, the Archery.

1246
01:46:39,532 --> 01:46:42,829
They would set two targets, alright!

1247
01:46:43,337 --> 01:46:48,119
They would stand next to the first target and they would shoot their arrows at this target

1248
01:46:49,269 --> 01:46:56,041
and then they would walk to the second target, pick up their arrows and shoot the first target.

1249
01:46:56,919 --> 01:47:01,465
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) said: I want you to walk fast between the targets.

1250
01:47:02,482 --> 01:47:06,504
Not only, are you training but I also want you to exercise walk fast.

1251
01:47:06,832 --> 01:47:14,045
So, Hudhaifah Bin Yaman(حذيفه بن يمان), he would run and then he said;

1252
01:47:14,393 --> 01:47:18,060
And I want you to jump on the horses while the horses are running.

1253
01:47:21,403 --> 01:47:25,690
These are lessons that he is sending it to his Military Generals.

1254
01:47:26,670 --> 01:47:32,497
The generals with the stars, who tends to develop big belly this is how, I want you to live.

1255
01:47:33,014 --> 01:47:35,885
When he says, you walk bare foot, it doesn't mean that you walk bare foot all the time

1256
01:47:36,499 --> 01:47:38,403
but sometimes to get that training.

1257
01:47:40,428 --> 01:47:44,141
To not always be under the shade, go under the sun,

1258
01:47:45,111 --> 01:47:48,413
you are already dark you will going to become darker that’s alright.

1259
01:47:48,437 --> 01:47:54,338
You will get married don't worry.

1260
01:47:54,686 --> 01:47:58,156
You will find a wife, it's alright.

1261
01:47:58,233 --> 01:48:06,031
Maybe the sister won't believe us but sometimes brothers would intentionally stay indoors,

1262
01:48:06,378 --> 01:48:08,030
so that they wouldn't develop a tan.

1263
01:48:09,917 --> 01:48:16,528
Stand under the sun because it is Humaam Al-Arab(حمام العرب) this is the bath of Arabs.

1264
01:48:18,629 --> 01:48:23,815
You know the other have these luxurious baths, the Greek, the Roman.

1265
01:48:25,333 --> 01:48:27,185
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) is saying our bath is the sun.

1266
01:48:30,522 --> 01:48:36,361
These were the strict orders to keep the military tradition alive.

1267
01:48:41,143 --> 01:48:44,470
So he wanted them to be active.

1268
01:48:49,245 --> 01:48:53,243
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) was told about a man of strength strong man,

1269
01:48:53,267 --> 01:48:57,063
who helps against the enemies of Allahعَزّوجَلّ but he had a problem.

1270
01:48:59,271 --> 01:49:04,789
He used to be an alcoholic, a Muslim in the times of Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب)

1271
01:49:05,763 --> 01:49:11,060
fighting Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله), loves Islam but he is addicted to alcohol.

1272
01:49:14,302 --> 01:49:16,642
So, they came to the Khalifah(خليفه) and said: What should we do?

1273
01:49:20,240 --> 01:49:23,341
He said, Give me the pen and paper.

1274
01:49:23,704 --> 01:49:25,744
He with his own hands, he writes a letter to him.

1275
01:49:27,024 --> 01:49:29,531
He says: Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) to so and so,

1276
01:49:30,102 --> 01:49:31,915
 peace be upon you, Salaam Alaika(سلام عليك).

1277
01:49:32,992 --> 01:49:35,418
I praise Allah to you that there is no god but He,

1278
01:49:39,867 --> 01:49:44,696
and then he writes down to him first three Ayats of Surah Ghafir(سورة الغافر).

1279
01:49:44,979 --> 01:49:52,432
Ha Meem "حم" The revelation of this book is from Allah, Exalted in Power full of knowledge.

1280
01:49:52,939 --> 01:49:57,665
غَافِرِ الذَّنْبِ وَقَابِلِ التَّوْبِ شَدِيدِ الْعِقَابِ ذِي الطَّوْلِ ۖ لَا إِلَٰهَ إِلَّا هُوَ ۖ إِلَيْهِ الْمَصِيرُ۝

1281
01:49:58,020 --> 01:50:04,182
Who forgives sins, accepts repentance, He is strict in punishment

1282
01:50:04,606 --> 01:50:11,723
and has a long reach in all things there is no god but He to Him is the final goal.

1283
01:50:14,087 --> 01:50:15,734
So, the man reads these Ayaat(آيات),

1284
01:50:16,306 --> 01:50:23,063
the Ayaat(آيات) are saying Allah is forgiving and it also says that Allah has a severe punishment.

1285
01:50:26,724 --> 01:50:28,899
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) gave this letter and said;

1286
01:50:29,068 --> 01:50:34,345
Make sure that when you deliver it to him he is sober because he was drunk most of the times.

1287
01:50:34,828 --> 01:50:36,761
Make sure when you deliver it to him he is sober.

1288
01:50:37,694 --> 01:50:40,660
So, they go to him and they gave him the letter and he reads it

1289
01:50:41,604 --> 01:50:42,924
and he says, Allah-O-Akbar(الله اكبر).

1290
01:50:43,324 --> 01:50:53,865
Allah is forgiving, Allah is merciful but Allah's punishment is severe and he cries and he makes Tawbah(توبه).

1291
01:50:55,426 --> 01:51:00,205
When Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) wrote the letter he asked everyone present

1292
01:51:00,801 --> 01:51:07,255
to make Dua(دُعَا) for that man and Allahعَزّوجَلّ accepted their Dua(دُعَا) and he repented.

1293
01:51:09,843 --> 01:51:13,416
When the news was brought back to Umar Ibn Al-Khattab رضي الله عنه, he said;

1294
01:51:14,006 --> 01:51:23,838
هَكَذَا فَسْمَعُ اِذَا رَاَيْتُمْ اَحَدُكُمْ ذَلَّةْ فَصَدِدُه’ وَدْعُوْلَه’ وَلَا تَكُوْنُوْ اَعْوَانً لِّشَّيَاطِيْنِ عَلَيْه

1295
01:51:24,787 --> 01:51:29,540
He said: This is how you treat one of you when they make a mistake

1296
01:51:30,528 --> 01:51:32,005
and you should make a Dua(دُعَا) for them

1297
01:51:32,458 --> 01:51:35,531
and you should not assist Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ) against them.

1298
01:51:37,312 --> 01:51:40,769
"Don't Assist Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ) against your Brothers".

1299
01:51:41,836 --> 01:51:50,272
By boycotting them, by being harsh against them, you are only turning them away from Islam.

1300
01:51:51,494 --> 01:51:53,826
And I think that and I am going to close it with this,

1301
01:51:54,299 --> 01:52:02,534
I think that this is very important story for the Muslims in the West.

1302
01:52:04,169 --> 01:52:09,267
There are Muslims who are on drugs, there are Muslims who drink.

1303
01:52:10,129 --> 01:52:11,735
There are Muslims who commit Zina(زنا).

1304
01:52:16,786 --> 01:52:22,714
Some of them want to get out of it and they are sincere but they are stuck

1305
01:52:23,670 --> 01:52:25,617
 because of the addiction it takes over

1306
01:52:28,106 --> 01:52:29,695
and they are unable to break free.

1307
01:52:31,174 --> 01:52:34,198
If you are harsh with them, you are only going to make it worse,

1308
01:52:35,444 --> 01:52:37,682
you have to lend them a helping hand.

1309
01:52:39,061 --> 01:52:44,733
And you have to be accommodating and don't be idealistic.

1310
01:52:45,027 --> 01:52:50,281
Don't say that because this is haram(حرام), these are Fusaaq(فساك), these are sinners,

1311
01:52:50,305 --> 01:52:53,831
these are corrupt keep them away from our Masajid(مساجد), stay away from them,

1312
01:52:54,104 --> 01:53:01,162
don't talk to them, if you don't then Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ) will talk to them.

1313
01:53:03,299 --> 01:53:11,069
So, hold your brothers and sisters by the hand and deliver them out of their misery.

1314
01:53:12,525 --> 01:53:15,919
They don't like it, many of them don't, who love! Who would love drugs?

1315
01:53:16,837 --> 01:53:19,200
When they know how it messes up their lives.

1316
01:53:20,625 --> 01:53:23,931
How it takes them out of their humanity, who would love to live like that?

1317
01:53:25,381 --> 01:53:26,325
But you need to help them.

1318
01:53:27,301 --> 01:53:32,160
We are talking about the time of Sahabah(صحابه) and they were understanding,

1319
01:53:32,866 --> 01:53:36,067
they were understanding, and that is "The Best Generation".

1320
01:53:36,805 --> 01:53:39,097
They weren't idealistic, they didn't say, No! this man,

1321
01:53:39,121 --> 01:53:44,402
he should be punished and throw him in jail, boycott him, No! He said: Lets help him.

1322
01:53:46,684 --> 01:53:52,510
So, please help your brothers and sisters because they are in great need.

1323
01:53:53,684 --> 01:54:00,778
We ask Allahعَزّوجَلّ to help us all, we ask Allah to grant us Tawbah(توبه), to accept our deeds,

1324
01:54:01,465 --> 01:54:05,232
 to forgive us, to reward us with Jannah(جنة), we seek refuge in Him from Hellfire.

1325
01:54:06,074 --> 01:54:10,699
وَصَلَّى الله عَلى سَيَّدِنَا محمد وَعَلى اَلِهِ وَ صَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ تَسْلِيْمًا كَثِيْرًا

1326
01:54:10,847 --> 01:54:15,033
IT SHUDDERS IN PAIN FREELY

1327
01:54:15,297 --> 01:54:19,480
MY CHASITY, MY MODESTY!

1328
01:54:19,504 --> 01:54:23,775
OH MUSLIM, YOU SAW

1329
01:54:23,879 --> 01:54:28,046
MY INJURY AND THE INJURY OF MY PRIDE

